[{"sha":"ce950dcf269af5b3864841926195ba5bd7609159","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGNlOTUwZGNmMjY5YWY1YjM4NjQ4NDE5MjYxOTViYTViZDc2MDkxNTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"joeflorencio-openai","email":"joeflorencio@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T17:07:24Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T17:36:22Z"},"message":"Add managed developer instructions to requirements (#39755)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add `additional_developer_instructions` to managed requirements and expose it through `configRequirements/read` as `additionalDeveloperInstructions`, independently of ordinary developer instructions.\n- Include the managed instructions in model context, emit explicit replacement or removal messages when requirements change, and preserve the current value across compaction, resume, and agent forks without duplication.\n- Reject managed instructions whose rendered context exceeds 10,000 estimated tokens.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Cover requirements layering and API serialization, context updates and removal, size validation, repeated model requests, compaction and resume, rollout migration, and agent forks.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: bc0b70fb7988944c2f68176dff55f5ed61eb46c8","tree":{"sha":"1c579ad02e3f5809c5b25e29ca4f007e993e2ed5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/1c579ad02e3f5809c5b25e29ca4f007e993e2ed5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/ce950dcf269af5b3864841926195ba5bd7609159","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ce950dcf269af5b3864841926195ba5bd7609159","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ce950dcf269af5b3864841926195ba5bd7609159","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ce950dcf269af5b3864841926195ba5bd7609159/comments","author":{"login":"joeflorencio-openai","id":195963627,"node_id":"U_kgDOC64q6w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/195963627?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/joeflorencio-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"85a1b0e33db92f94f02e54484b0ef1d0db1050f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/85a1b0e33db92f94f02e54484b0ef1d0db1050f6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/85a1b0e33db92f94f02e54484b0ef1d0db1050f6"}]},{"sha":"85a1b0e33db92f94f02e54484b0ef1d0db1050f6","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDg1YTFiMGUzM2RiOTJmOTRmMDJlNTQ0ODRiMGVmMWQwZGIxMDUwZjY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Sean Huang","email":"seanh@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T17:06:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T17:25:14Z"},"message":"Expose uncompiled permission profile selection (#39752)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add `resolve_permission_profile_selection` to select the effective profile using configured defaults, managed requirements, and allowlists.\n- Return the merged configured and managed profile catalog without compiling platform-specific paths, leaving path interpretation to the executor.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Verify that a managed default overrides a configured default while preserving Windows-style paths.\n- Verify that an allowlisted but undefined profile is rejected.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 0172193d48f0346522f931d3b806054895d199c0","tree":{"sha":"fd80cd428f9e6c7b498eaa4b3254fa40ce7845c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/fd80cd428f9e6c7b498eaa4b3254fa40ce7845c8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/85a1b0e33db92f94f02e54484b0ef1d0db1050f6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/85a1b0e33db92f94f02e54484b0ef1d0db1050f6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/85a1b0e33db92f94f02e54484b0ef1d0db1050f6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/85a1b0e33db92f94f02e54484b0ef1d0db1050f6/comments","author":{"login":"seanh-oai","id":309889850,"node_id":"U_kgDOEniLOg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/309889850?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanh-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/seanh-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanh-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanh-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanh-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanh-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanh-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanh-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanh-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanh-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanh-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"a26d50852ae66cc697605f9a05fc97771fdf2882","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a26d50852ae66cc697605f9a05fc97771fdf2882","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a26d50852ae66cc697605f9a05fc97771fdf2882"}]},{"sha":"a26d50852ae66cc697605f9a05fc97771fdf2882","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGEyNmQ1MDg1MmFlNjZjYzY5NzYwNWY5YTA1ZmM5Nzc3MWZkZjI4ODI","commit":{"author":{"name":"cgst-oai","email":"cgs@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T17:05:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T17:16:52Z"},"message":"Require filesystem backends to implement directory walks (#39749)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Make `ExecutorFileSystem::walk` a required backend operation instead of\n  providing a fallback built from directory reads and metadata requests.\n- Implement bounded local walks on a blocking task with cancellation, symlink\n  cycle detection, deterministic ordering, error collection, and response-size\n  limits.\n- Have remote filesystems use the server's walk operation directly.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Cover local and remote handling of invalid roots and limits, directory\n  symlinks, non-UTF-8 names, cancellation, sandbox contexts, and response\n  budgets.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 7499bf05080c3f9965a5eb7ffd593de604d62c2a","tree":{"sha":"2a6d24feb870bfb5dad79536b04b9f9d5c562884","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2a6d24feb870bfb5dad79536b04b9f9d5c562884"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a26d50852ae66cc697605f9a05fc97771fdf2882","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a26d50852ae66cc697605f9a05fc97771fdf2882","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a26d50852ae66cc697605f9a05fc97771fdf2882","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a26d50852ae66cc697605f9a05fc97771fdf2882/comments","author":{"login":"cgst-oai","id":289842246,"node_id":"U_kgDOEUakRg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/289842246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cgst-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/cgst-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cgst-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cgst-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cgst-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cgst-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cgst-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cgst-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cgst-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cgst-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cgst-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"2e1f18e0dbb88fd464c1a57e00bd9ed6b940801a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2e1f18e0dbb88fd464c1a57e00bd9ed6b940801a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2e1f18e0dbb88fd464c1a57e00bd9ed6b940801a"}]},{"sha":"2e1f18e0dbb88fd464c1a57e00bd9ed6b940801a","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDJlMWYxOGUwZGJiODhmZDQ2NGMxYTU3ZTAwYmQ5ZWQ2Yjk0MDgwMWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"sayan-oai","email":"sayan@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T17:02:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T17:12:15Z"},"message":"Refresh resumed thread capability roots from executors (#39746)\n\n## Why\n\nResumed threads can carry a persisted capability-root location that no longer\nmatches the location reported by the attached executor.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Refresh matching thread-owned capability roots from the live environment while\n  preserving persisted roots when the executor reports none.\n- Use the same merge behavior for capability-root inspection and per-step MCP\n  resolution, without changing owner-configured root precedence.\n\n## Testing\n\nExtend the remote-environment resume test to cover both an executor-provided\nreplacement root and the persisted-root fallback.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 0c66195b2406f431a2e156e00d5225a8d22d18b2","tree":{"sha":"3a79ba17ec4fb5be33d24e090c13373b033fa7f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/3a79ba17ec4fb5be33d24e090c13373b033fa7f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/2e1f18e0dbb88fd464c1a57e00bd9ed6b940801a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2e1f18e0dbb88fd464c1a57e00bd9ed6b940801a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2e1f18e0dbb88fd464c1a57e00bd9ed6b940801a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2e1f18e0dbb88fd464c1a57e00bd9ed6b940801a/comments","author":{"login":"sayan-oai","id":244841968,"node_id":"U_kgDODpf98A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244841968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/sayan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"c3db1804933dfadcd55e48660f7ce51104498f82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c3db1804933dfadcd55e48660f7ce51104498f82","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c3db1804933dfadcd55e48660f7ce51104498f82"}]},{"sha":"c3db1804933dfadcd55e48660f7ce51104498f82","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGMzZGIxODA0OTMzZGZhZGNkNTVlNDg2NjBmN2NlNTExMDQ0OThmODI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Benjamin Carlsson","email":"bc@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T16:43:51Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T17:00:05Z"},"message":"Skip postprocessing for short composer input (#39744)\n\n## What changed\n\nReturn the initial wrapping ranges directly when the composer input produces a\nsingle line and its byte length is less than the available width. This avoids\nthe additional grapheme and word-boundary pass for input that cannot wrap.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 55d990a354fcc61e9a90d5796b4b39d16742cc50","tree":{"sha":"f1b52ea041489d9f6b64abdf97378340801e4bfc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f1b52ea041489d9f6b64abdf97378340801e4bfc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c3db1804933dfadcd55e48660f7ce51104498f82","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c3db1804933dfadcd55e48660f7ce51104498f82","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c3db1804933dfadcd55e48660f7ce51104498f82","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c3db1804933dfadcd55e48660f7ce51104498f82/comments","author":{"login":"bc-openai","id":185964850,"node_id":"U_kgDOCxWZMg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/185964850?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/bc-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"4f38432d8709bb5f46eca72e9f372cbe2967fefc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4f38432d8709bb5f46eca72e9f372cbe2967fefc","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4f38432d8709bb5f46eca72e9f372cbe2967fefc"}]},{"sha":"4f38432d8709bb5f46eca72e9f372cbe2967fefc","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDRmMzg0MzJkODcwOWJiNWY0NmVjYTcyZTlmMzcyY2JlMjk2N2ZlZmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"rhan-oai","email":"rhan@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T16:41:21Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T16:52:16Z"},"message":"Use model-specific auto-review outcome instructions (#39741)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add `rejection_instructions` and `timeout_instructions` to catalog-provided auto-review messages.\n- Use the acting model's instructions for denied and timed-out reviews across tool approvals, shell escalation, and MCP elicitation responses.\n- Fall back to the existing instructions only when a catalog value is absent, while preserving explicit empty-string overrides.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Cover catalog overrides, legacy fallbacks, empty values, and separation between acting-model and reviewer-model messages.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: c5b2c2dbdaefd45d1d658651dd1abaeb6d8c93da","tree":{"sha":"7bdf13108058dfb9701b6c0d99e6489a06e70e7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/7bdf13108058dfb9701b6c0d99e6489a06e70e7d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/4f38432d8709bb5f46eca72e9f372cbe2967fefc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4f38432d8709bb5f46eca72e9f372cbe2967fefc","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4f38432d8709bb5f46eca72e9f372cbe2967fefc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4f38432d8709bb5f46eca72e9f372cbe2967fefc/comments","author":{"login":"rhan-oai","id":214716640,"node_id":"U_kgDODMxQ4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214716640?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rhan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"88da5520d41cb05253b9a4b2908d6a028a810ad1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/88da5520d41cb05253b9a4b2908d6a028a810ad1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/88da5520d41cb05253b9a4b2908d6a028a810ad1"}]},{"sha":"88da5520d41cb05253b9a4b2908d6a028a810ad1","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDg4ZGE1NTIwZDQxY2IwNTI1M2I5YTRiMjkwOGQ2YTAyOGE4MTBhZDE","commit":{"author":{"name":"felixxia-oai","email":"felixxia@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T16:36:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T16:45:59Z"},"message":"Honor Guardian runtime settings from model defaults (#39738)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add `max_tool_call_lag`, `reuse_parent_compaction`, and transcript\n  `include_images` to the Guardian model configuration.\n- Inherit these settings from model defaults while preserving explicit local\n  overrides.\n- Enable image capture for Node REPL review evidence when transcript images are\n  included.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Cover inheritance and local override precedence for the new settings.\n- Verify that enabling transcript images initializes review-evidence capture.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 7c1965c2ec00a78a0436fa916b630be0004dbb51","tree":{"sha":"31a956d7aab8c858e8d93290223baea4d76b505a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/31a956d7aab8c858e8d93290223baea4d76b505a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/88da5520d41cb05253b9a4b2908d6a028a810ad1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/88da5520d41cb05253b9a4b2908d6a028a810ad1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/88da5520d41cb05253b9a4b2908d6a028a810ad1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/88da5520d41cb05253b9a4b2908d6a028a810ad1/comments","author":{"login":"felixxia-oai","id":288149840,"node_id":"U_kgDOESzRUA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/288149840?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/felixxia-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"8c828b18d631c0b5efb2ba66bc6fa151fff9da6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8c828b18d631c0b5efb2ba66bc6fa151fff9da6c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8c828b18d631c0b5efb2ba66bc6fa151fff9da6c"}]},{"sha":"8c828b18d631c0b5efb2ba66bc6fa151fff9da6c","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDhjODI4YjE4ZDYzMWMwYjVlZmIyYmE2NmJjNmZhMTUxZmZmOWRhNmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"rhan-oai","email":"rhan@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T16:15:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T16:22:45Z"},"message":"Remove private executor directory creation (#39736)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Create remote plugin metrics directories through the standard executor filesystem API.\n- Remove the `private` directory-creation protocol option and its platform-specific handling.\n- Update the executor temporary-directory documentation to describe child-visible sidecars without an owner-private guarantee.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 9a8532403a3ad2bf998281735be0b668893918c9","tree":{"sha":"c26468baa079b330aff44ed7ef45b7f2066ab0a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c26468baa079b330aff44ed7ef45b7f2066ab0a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8c828b18d631c0b5efb2ba66bc6fa151fff9da6c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8c828b18d631c0b5efb2ba66bc6fa151fff9da6c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8c828b18d631c0b5efb2ba66bc6fa151fff9da6c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8c828b18d631c0b5efb2ba66bc6fa151fff9da6c/comments","author":{"login":"rhan-oai","id":214716640,"node_id":"U_kgDODMxQ4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214716640?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rhan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"bf2aee99c58362d3f588d98432dcbc7adc371c73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bf2aee99c58362d3f588d98432dcbc7adc371c73","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bf2aee99c58362d3f588d98432dcbc7adc371c73"}]},{"sha":"bf2aee99c58362d3f588d98432dcbc7adc371c73","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGJmMmFlZTk5YzU4MzYyZDNmNTg4ZDk4NDMyZGNiYzdhZGMzNzFjNzM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Charlie Marsh","email":"charliemarsh@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T15:36:25Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T15:42:40Z"},"message":"Avoid rollout reads for configured TUI sessions (#39731)\n\n## Why\n\nA newly started thread may not have materialized its rollout before the TUI\nreceives `ThreadStarted`. Trying to infer session state from that path can wait\nthrough rollout reader retries even when a lifecycle response already provided\nthe authoritative session.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Preserve session state already stored for a known thread instead of inferring\n  it again from `ThreadStarted`.\n- Continue updating agent-picker metadata from the notification.\n- Restrict fallback session inference to newly observed `ThreadStarted`\n  notifications that do not already have session state.\n\n## Testing\n\nAdded a startup test that verifies a known thread routes `ThreadStarted`\nimmediately, retains its configured session, buffers the notification, and\nupdates agent metadata when the rollout does not exist yet.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 7ed98fb46df17566c4a61ac677f60fc8d94f7321","tree":{"sha":"3dd0f60dc12843c5ab06203bcaa31c9a39c59ef3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/3dd0f60dc12843c5ab06203bcaa31c9a39c59ef3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/bf2aee99c58362d3f588d98432dcbc7adc371c73","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bf2aee99c58362d3f588d98432dcbc7adc371c73","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bf2aee99c58362d3f588d98432dcbc7adc371c73","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bf2aee99c58362d3f588d98432dcbc7adc371c73/comments","author":{"login":"charliemarsh-oai","id":282065134,"node_id":"U_kgDOEM_47g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282065134?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/charliemarsh-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"9bf673718a4605b49e47d00762121d372af95439","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9bf673718a4605b49e47d00762121d372af95439","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9bf673718a4605b49e47d00762121d372af95439"}]},{"sha":"9bf673718a4605b49e47d00762121d372af95439","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDliZjY3MzcxOGE0NjA1YjQ5ZTQ3ZDAwNzYyMTIxZDM3MmFmOTU0Mzk","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T14:48:47Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T14:55:08Z"},"message":"Box the WebSocket dial future (#39726)\n\n## What changed\n\nBox `dialer::connect` before awaiting it in `WebSocketConnector::connect`,\nerasing the dialer's concrete future type at the connector boundary.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 617a2e4fd5bd61a408281973452e7b71b104bff2","tree":{"sha":"383ebc4046f9127bee72cbcd5ddd5b5f78740338","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/383ebc4046f9127bee72cbcd5ddd5b5f78740338"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/9bf673718a4605b49e47d00762121d372af95439","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9bf673718a4605b49e47d00762121d372af95439","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9bf673718a4605b49e47d00762121d372af95439","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9bf673718a4605b49e47d00762121d372af95439/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"9894a14c81e50bbd845a337e4f77293f1cbc2633","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9894a14c81e50bbd845a337e4f77293f1cbc2633","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9894a14c81e50bbd845a337e4f77293f1cbc2633"}]},{"sha":"9894a14c81e50bbd845a337e4f77293f1cbc2633","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDk4OTRhMTRjODFlNTBiYmQ4NDVhMzM3ZTRmNzcyOTNmMWNiYzI2MzM","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T14:28:15Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T14:33:55Z"},"message":"Track multi-agent v2 spawn calls in analytics (#39722)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Emit started and completed collaboration tool events for multi-agent v2\n  `spawn_agent` calls, including failed invocations.\n- Record execution duration and successful child-agent configuration metadata\n  without including the spawn prompt.\n- Deduplicate collaboration and subagent activity items by call ID when\n  calculating per-turn subagent tool counts.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Extend the app-server multi-agent v2 integration test to cover successful\n  and failed spawn telemetry, duration, prompt omission, and turn counts.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: c1c2fb9cc2a1a9b0f63ef68509ad36d11a92d1e5","tree":{"sha":"1239ce212ade39edda27a40ee2667b285c16f7fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/1239ce212ade39edda27a40ee2667b285c16f7fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/9894a14c81e50bbd845a337e4f77293f1cbc2633","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9894a14c81e50bbd845a337e4f77293f1cbc2633","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9894a14c81e50bbd845a337e4f77293f1cbc2633","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9894a14c81e50bbd845a337e4f77293f1cbc2633/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"1674b0a130987522de3f34d080b793585a355da1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1674b0a130987522de3f34d080b793585a355da1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1674b0a130987522de3f34d080b793585a355da1"}]},{"sha":"1674b0a130987522de3f34d080b793585a355da1","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDE2NzRiMGExMzA5ODc1MjJkZTNmMzRkMDgwYjc5MzU4NWEzNTVkYTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"rafael-oai","email":"rafael@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T13:57:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T14:13:56Z"},"message":"Expose managed policy for browser settings imports (#39720)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add `in_app_browser.allow_external_browser_settings_import` to managed requirements, preserving explicit Boolean values through layered composition while leaving an omitted value unset.\n- Return the policy as `inAppBrowser.allowExternalBrowserSettingsImport` from `configRequirements/read` and include it in the generated protocol schemas.\n- Keep the import policy independent from the in-app browser feature flag and agent Browser Use requirements.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Cover parsing, managed-layer precedence, invalid values, user and session override resistance, and app-server response serialization.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: efa2621d2b1cf503f1bee2505d9914cb4fb7221d","tree":{"sha":"746c5793ceb9e121b7f999fb8397f0d723aed7e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/746c5793ceb9e121b7f999fb8397f0d723aed7e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/1674b0a130987522de3f34d080b793585a355da1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1674b0a130987522de3f34d080b793585a355da1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1674b0a130987522de3f34d080b793585a355da1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1674b0a130987522de3f34d080b793585a355da1/comments","author":{"login":"rafael-oai","id":263776387,"node_id":"U_kgDOD7jogw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/263776387?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafael-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rafael-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafael-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafael-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafael-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafael-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafael-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafael-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafael-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafael-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafael-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"6d020311f0f883ddf8c4622d36533527800ee905","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6d020311f0f883ddf8c4622d36533527800ee905","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6d020311f0f883ddf8c4622d36533527800ee905"}]},{"sha":"6d020311f0f883ddf8c4622d36533527800ee905","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDZkMDIwMzExZjBmODgzZGRmOGM0NjIyZDM2NTMzNTI3ODAwZWU5MDU","commit":{"author":{"name":"William Woodruff","email":"ww@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T13:54:33Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T14:08:18Z"},"message":"Stop persisting checkout credentials in V8 workflows (#39719)\n\n## What changed\n\nSet `persist-credentials: false` for the V8 canary repository checkout and\nfor the `rusty_v8` checkouts in both the canary and release workflows.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: b4ccca7c7edf4e038b7b84c83f83d1416f655f65","tree":{"sha":"c8f1a444e1115d6536906b05d6aaf6fb224df13a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c8f1a444e1115d6536906b05d6aaf6fb224df13a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/6d020311f0f883ddf8c4622d36533527800ee905","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6d020311f0f883ddf8c4622d36533527800ee905","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6d020311f0f883ddf8c4622d36533527800ee905","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6d020311f0f883ddf8c4622d36533527800ee905/comments","author":{"login":"ww-oai","id":282066751,"node_id":"U_kgDOEM__Pw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282066751?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ww-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/ww-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ww-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ww-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ww-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ww-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ww-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ww-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ww-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ww-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ww-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"2c74b56fcde8a4f32c44701b7e6452e4c526f9e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2c74b56fcde8a4f32c44701b7e6452e4c526f9e6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2c74b56fcde8a4f32c44701b7e6452e4c526f9e6"}]},{"sha":"2c74b56fcde8a4f32c44701b7e6452e4c526f9e6","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDJjNzRiNTZmY2RlOGE0ZjMyYzQ0NzAxYjdlNjQ1MmU0YzUyNmY5ZTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"William Woodruff","email":"ww@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T13:54:32Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T14:02:13Z"},"message":"Pass CI workflow inputs through environment variables (#39717)\n\n## Why\n\nEmbedding reusable-workflow inputs directly in shell scripts can cause their\ncontents to be interpreted as shell syntax.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Export the Rust nextest target, profile, and test-thread inputs as environment\n  variables before using them in Bash commands and paths.\n- Pass the MSVC target and host architecture to PowerShell through environment\n  variables.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: f96bbeeb7b556022e4bdea9db384a88f925050bf","tree":{"sha":"f9722d608f99f4df509dbd6a02a8086bbbe855ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f9722d608f99f4df509dbd6a02a8086bbbe855ad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/2c74b56fcde8a4f32c44701b7e6452e4c526f9e6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2c74b56fcde8a4f32c44701b7e6452e4c526f9e6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2c74b56fcde8a4f32c44701b7e6452e4c526f9e6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2c74b56fcde8a4f32c44701b7e6452e4c526f9e6/comments","author":{"login":"ww-oai","id":282066751,"node_id":"U_kgDOEM__Pw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282066751?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ww-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/ww-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ww-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ww-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ww-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ww-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ww-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ww-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ww-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ww-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ww-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"4a942885c8b4745757a9f86ad2075e16c42483c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4a942885c8b4745757a9f86ad2075e16c42483c5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4a942885c8b4745757a9f86ad2075e16c42483c5"}]},{"sha":"4a942885c8b4745757a9f86ad2075e16c42483c5","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDRhOTQyODg1YzhiNDc0NTc1N2E5Zjg2YWQyMDc1ZTE2YzQyNDgzYzU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Tamir Duberstein","email":"tamird@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T13:11:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T13:17:20Z"},"message":"Reduce unified exec output buffer allocations (#39712)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Accept borrowed byte slices when appending output chunks, avoiding clones before\n  forwarding those chunks to streaming consumers.\n- Merge drained head-tail buffers by reusing their owned storage while preserving\n  the retained prefix, latest suffix, and omitted-byte count.\n- Make unified exec output handles capacity-generic so bounded-output tests can\n  exercise repeated drains with small buffers.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Update head-tail buffer and process manager tests to cover chunk retention,\n  omission accounting, and repeated output drains with the new APIs.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: caa9813d3c9d9921cff28888263a212def381640","tree":{"sha":"2cccaffb6c84402a1bf4a7d2b815d329d8334bd3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2cccaffb6c84402a1bf4a7d2b815d329d8334bd3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/4a942885c8b4745757a9f86ad2075e16c42483c5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4a942885c8b4745757a9f86ad2075e16c42483c5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4a942885c8b4745757a9f86ad2075e16c42483c5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4a942885c8b4745757a9f86ad2075e16c42483c5/comments","author":{"login":"tamird","id":1535036,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MzUwMzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1535036?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird","html_url":"https://github.com/tamird","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"59f7da58d6ae8401304554f807023610181f65f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/59f7da58d6ae8401304554f807023610181f65f0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/59f7da58d6ae8401304554f807023610181f65f0"}]},{"sha":"59f7da58d6ae8401304554f807023610181f65f0","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDU5ZjdkYTU4ZDZhZTg0MDEzMDQ1NTRmODA3MDIzNjEwMTgxZjY1ZjA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Tamir Duberstein","email":"tamird@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T12:12:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T12:17:44Z"},"message":"Log TUI app event variants without their payloads (#39709)\n\n## Why\n\nThe TUI session logger is meant to record only the variant for unhandled app\nevents. Parsing `Debug` output removed tuple payloads but retained fields from\nstruct variants.\n\n## What changed\n\nDerive `IntoStaticStr` for `AppEvent` and use that conversion when recording\nfallback `app_event` entries, so the `variant` field consistently contains only\nthe enum variant name.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 5b539f414269c6b001e69cf9496db5b49aceb759","tree":{"sha":"8cf3204aa5855708f3a08461e6b7e1c80ea67412","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/8cf3204aa5855708f3a08461e6b7e1c80ea67412"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/59f7da58d6ae8401304554f807023610181f65f0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/59f7da58d6ae8401304554f807023610181f65f0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/59f7da58d6ae8401304554f807023610181f65f0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/59f7da58d6ae8401304554f807023610181f65f0/comments","author":{"login":"tamird","id":1535036,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MzUwMzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1535036?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird","html_url":"https://github.com/tamird","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"3675fe014b2106e6e87673bf9e464e4a7e945915","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3675fe014b2106e6e87673bf9e464e4a7e945915","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3675fe014b2106e6e87673bf9e464e4a7e945915"}]},{"sha":"3675fe014b2106e6e87673bf9e464e4a7e945915","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDM2NzVmZTAxNGIyMTA2ZTZlODc2NzNiZjllNDY0ZTRhN2U5NDU5MTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"felixxia-oai","email":"felixxia@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T11:47:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T12:12:53Z"},"message":"Remove redundant code mode image helper test (#39707)\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 38bf61c1d71827d65a7824318911ac0e9f2756bb","tree":{"sha":"ba1b0e16a6dcaf5e4d2ffbdec8331fe0cb7dc5d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/ba1b0e16a6dcaf5e4d2ffbdec8331fe0cb7dc5d1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/3675fe014b2106e6e87673bf9e464e4a7e945915","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3675fe014b2106e6e87673bf9e464e4a7e945915","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3675fe014b2106e6e87673bf9e464e4a7e945915","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3675fe014b2106e6e87673bf9e464e4a7e945915/comments","author":{"login":"felixxia-oai","id":288149840,"node_id":"U_kgDOESzRUA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/288149840?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/felixxia-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"02de49f7183d30cc72bdb83b64816392c29a908c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/02de49f7183d30cc72bdb83b64816392c29a908c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/02de49f7183d30cc72bdb83b64816392c29a908c"}]},{"sha":"02de49f7183d30cc72bdb83b64816392c29a908c","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDAyZGU0OWY3MTgzZDMwY2M3MmJkYjgzYjY0ODE2MzkyYzI5YTkwOGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T11:47:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T12:08:35Z"},"message":"Harden Seatbelt writable root path binding (#39706)\n\n## Why\n\nResolving attacker-mutable path components while preparing a Seatbelt profile can let a writable root be rebound to a different location before the sandbox is applied. File roots also need to remain confined to the file itself rather than granting access to descendants after replacement.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Preserve mutable components of writable-root paths until Seatbelt binds them, while still normalizing trusted top-level aliases such as `/tmp`.\n- Use literal grants for existing file and device roots, and subpath grants for directories and missing roots.\n- Exclude both logical and resolved forms of protected subpaths so symlinked metadata directories remain read-only.\n\n## Testing\n\nAdd coverage for ancestor rebinding, file-root symlink and directory replacement, missing directory roots, top-level aliases, and symlinked metadata carveouts.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 63c00e44dd30766e873b8acdad09d6657657fad9","tree":{"sha":"285b0f95ce7d65a58f57d8f546312103f2c1073e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/285b0f95ce7d65a58f57d8f546312103f2c1073e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/02de49f7183d30cc72bdb83b64816392c29a908c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/02de49f7183d30cc72bdb83b64816392c29a908c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/02de49f7183d30cc72bdb83b64816392c29a908c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/02de49f7183d30cc72bdb83b64816392c29a908c/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"37a9da9901c5fa417896af8840ba27dffe4f1ca1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/37a9da9901c5fa417896af8840ba27dffe4f1ca1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/37a9da9901c5fa417896af8840ba27dffe4f1ca1"}]},{"sha":"37a9da9901c5fa417896af8840ba27dffe4f1ca1","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDM3YTlkYTk5MDFjNWZhNDE3ODk2YWY4ODQwYmEyN2RmZmU0ZjFjYTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"felixxia-oai","email":"felixxia@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T11:47:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T12:02:42Z"},"message":"Move the global scope check into the code-mode runtime (#39703)\n\n## What changed\n\nReplace the core integration test for allowed `globalThis` properties with an\nin-process code-mode runtime test. The test continues to fail when the runtime\nexposes a global outside the allowlist without requiring the core network test\nharness.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: f33846ae2bb35e6779b5bec0a3f0ba5729eb707d","tree":{"sha":"aab067b592fef490b2015519aef40db7c50eb52f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/aab067b592fef490b2015519aef40db7c50eb52f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/37a9da9901c5fa417896af8840ba27dffe4f1ca1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/37a9da9901c5fa417896af8840ba27dffe4f1ca1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/37a9da9901c5fa417896af8840ba27dffe4f1ca1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/37a9da9901c5fa417896af8840ba27dffe4f1ca1/comments","author":{"login":"felixxia-oai","id":288149840,"node_id":"U_kgDOESzRUA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/288149840?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/felixxia-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"585b97d394aa09d187ac37dc87b40250f5c77944","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/585b97d394aa09d187ac37dc87b40250f5c77944","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/585b97d394aa09d187ac37dc87b40250f5c77944"}]},{"sha":"585b97d394aa09d187ac37dc87b40250f5c77944","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDU4NWI5N2QzOTRhYTA5ZDE4N2FjMzdkYzg3YjQwMjUwZjVjNzc5NDQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"felixxia-oai","email":"felixxia@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T11:47:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T11:57:32Z"},"message":"Wait for turn completion events in multi-agent resume tests (#39702)\n\n## What changed\n\nUse the shared `wait_for_event` helper to wait for `TurnComplete` from initial\nand reloaded worker threads before checking their requests. This replaces\nmanual polling of `AgentStatus` with two-second deadlines.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 862884afae9969aacf0f53c5c24cf8b72f8d078a","tree":{"sha":"df7e02645eea1d06beddca3780fb1787f4b64090","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/df7e02645eea1d06beddca3780fb1787f4b64090"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/585b97d394aa09d187ac37dc87b40250f5c77944","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/585b97d394aa09d187ac37dc87b40250f5c77944","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/585b97d394aa09d187ac37dc87b40250f5c77944","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/585b97d394aa09d187ac37dc87b40250f5c77944/comments","author":{"login":"felixxia-oai","id":288149840,"node_id":"U_kgDOESzRUA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/288149840?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/felixxia-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"f277e313f1ce6f5ea02792fb48e1093a5540ecfc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f277e313f1ce6f5ea02792fb48e1093a5540ecfc","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f277e313f1ce6f5ea02792fb48e1093a5540ecfc"}]},{"sha":"f277e313f1ce6f5ea02792fb48e1093a5540ecfc","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGYyNzdlMzEzZjFjZTZmNWVhMDI3OTJmYjQ4ZTEwOTNhNTU0MGVjZmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T11:47:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T11:52:46Z"},"message":"Fail closed on unsafe config and sed parsing (#39700)\n\n## Why\n\nUnsupported untrusted approval policies must remain startup errors even when\napp-server is allowed to fall back from other invalid configuration. Likewise,\ncompound command summaries must not discard a `sed` stage that can edit files\nin place.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Propagate `UnsupportedUntrustedApprovalPolicyError` from both app-server\n  configuration loads instead of replacing it with default configuration.\n- Parse `sed` options through `--`, option arguments, combined short flags, and\n  backup suffixes so `-i`/`--in-place` commands remain unknown actions.\n- Keep non-mutating `sed` operands after `--` from being mistaken for flags.\n\n## Testing\n\nAdded parser coverage for in-place `sed` variants in compound commands and for\ndash-prefixed operands after `--`.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 112ead912e10fcb6c7dd0ede4bf84e390af82da8","tree":{"sha":"7a78cb9bfe99ae78ad7a8e2ae5c8605ec11b84d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/7a78cb9bfe99ae78ad7a8e2ae5c8605ec11b84d9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f277e313f1ce6f5ea02792fb48e1093a5540ecfc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f277e313f1ce6f5ea02792fb48e1093a5540ecfc","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f277e313f1ce6f5ea02792fb48e1093a5540ecfc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f277e313f1ce6f5ea02792fb48e1093a5540ecfc/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"478dbe9df0a33141d265db5977947cc432e7fe85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/478dbe9df0a33141d265db5977947cc432e7fe85","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/478dbe9df0a33141d265db5977947cc432e7fe85"}]},{"sha":"478dbe9df0a33141d265db5977947cc432e7fe85","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDQ3OGRiZTlkZjBhMzMxNDFkMjY1ZGI1OTc3OTQ3Y2M0MzJlN2ZlODU","commit":{"author":{"name":"felixxia-oai","email":"felixxia@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T10:41:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T10:57:03Z"},"message":"Make Guardian v2 parent compaction reuse configurable (#39691)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add `features.guardianv2.reuse_parent_compaction`, defaulting to `true` to preserve existing behavior.\n- When disabled, omit parent compaction items from Guardian v2 contributor requests.\n- Cover configuration parsing and disabled-reuse request construction.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 0cf7c0ac7a2567c9f73a3f9724df6f6a6170e995","tree":{"sha":"495e563c062eb2bf99772be4e8a6b05e795c87c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/495e563c062eb2bf99772be4e8a6b05e795c87c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/478dbe9df0a33141d265db5977947cc432e7fe85","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/478dbe9df0a33141d265db5977947cc432e7fe85","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/478dbe9df0a33141d265db5977947cc432e7fe85","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/478dbe9df0a33141d265db5977947cc432e7fe85/comments","author":{"login":"felixxia-oai","id":288149840,"node_id":"U_kgDOESzRUA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/288149840?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/felixxia-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"312b62ac95335e1762b70ceb8910374965bd2785","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/312b62ac95335e1762b70ceb8910374965bd2785","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/312b62ac95335e1762b70ceb8910374965bd2785"}]},{"sha":"312b62ac95335e1762b70ceb8910374965bd2785","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDMxMmI2MmFjOTUzMzVlMTc2MmI3MGNlYjg5MTAzNzQ5NjViZDI3ODU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ben Romano","email":"bromano@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T06:34:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T08:36:00Z"},"message":"Trace MCP runtime refresh coordination (#39667)\n\n## What changed\n\nAdd named tracing spans for MCP dirty-state refreshes and time spent waiting\nto acquire the refresh semaphore.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 1dbb3572d2061581beb83b3de098d6ec91791104","tree":{"sha":"5516437c5d4d1c7c0c0df47faff695cce58fa932","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/5516437c5d4d1c7c0c0df47faff695cce58fa932"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/312b62ac95335e1762b70ceb8910374965bd2785","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/312b62ac95335e1762b70ceb8910374965bd2785","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/312b62ac95335e1762b70ceb8910374965bd2785","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/312b62ac95335e1762b70ceb8910374965bd2785/comments","author":{"login":"bromano-oai","id":238086823,"node_id":"U_kgDODjDqpw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/238086823?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bromano-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/bromano-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bromano-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bromano-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bromano-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bromano-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bromano-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bromano-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bromano-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bromano-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bromano-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"2584e88cadc15779ebddb2e5ca87f12478d6b3ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2584e88cadc15779ebddb2e5ca87f12478d6b3ad","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2584e88cadc15779ebddb2e5ca87f12478d6b3ad"}]},{"sha":"2584e88cadc15779ebddb2e5ca87f12478d6b3ad","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDI1ODRlODhjYWRjMTU3NzllYmRkYjJlNWNhODdmMTI0NzhkNmIzYWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T06:02:05Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T08:32:11Z"},"message":"Improve no-follow filesystem behavior across platforms (#39666)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Use `statx` for no-follow metadata on Linux so `created_at_ms` includes the birth time when the filesystem provides it, with a fallback for unavailable or blocked `statx` calls.\n- Mark files and directories for deletion explicitly on Windows after opening them without traversing reparse points.\n- Cover create, write, metadata, remove, and link-rejection behavior for local and remote filesystems, including sandboxed execution on Linux and Windows.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Add Linux coverage for preserving birth time in no-follow metadata.\n- Add cross-platform coverage for sandboxed no-follow operations and removal of files and empty directories.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 1bc531669839bf5d033aa4a215220ed1cc5f63d5","tree":{"sha":"2331ad68d6cafe33ec2b99f9e54fe264358e42f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2331ad68d6cafe33ec2b99f9e54fe264358e42f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/2584e88cadc15779ebddb2e5ca87f12478d6b3ad","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2584e88cadc15779ebddb2e5ca87f12478d6b3ad","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2584e88cadc15779ebddb2e5ca87f12478d6b3ad","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2584e88cadc15779ebddb2e5ca87f12478d6b3ad/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"fec2dccfcfe147aff064b5cddb46c0a0559ff441","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fec2dccfcfe147aff064b5cddb46c0a0559ff441","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/fec2dccfcfe147aff064b5cddb46c0a0559ff441"}]},{"sha":"fec2dccfcfe147aff064b5cddb46c0a0559ff441","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGZlYzJkY2NmY2ZlMTQ3YWZmMDY0YjVjZGRiNDZjMGEwNTU5ZmY0NDE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Dylan Hurd","email":"dylan.hurd@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T05:54:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T08:28:35Z"},"message":"Add macOS Seatbelt filesystem integration tests (#39665)\n\n## What changed\n\nAdd macOS-only integration coverage that runs commands under the production\nSeatbelt policy and verifies:\n\n- deny globs protect matching files, directory ancestors, symlink aliases, and\n  paths created after policy application;\n- protected directories cannot be moved, replaced, or exchanged across\n  writable roots; and\n- standard read-only and workspace-write profiles continue to allow expected\n  filesystem operations.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 1f666835ee402bedd1d32e87f1082eaaf7b7bf6a","tree":{"sha":"5a274c59f94ec45aec0968528ec781ab0756f21e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/5a274c59f94ec45aec0968528ec781ab0756f21e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/fec2dccfcfe147aff064b5cddb46c0a0559ff441","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fec2dccfcfe147aff064b5cddb46c0a0559ff441","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/fec2dccfcfe147aff064b5cddb46c0a0559ff441","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fec2dccfcfe147aff064b5cddb46c0a0559ff441/comments","author":{"login":"dylan-hurd-oai","id":220976066,"node_id":"U_kgDODSvTwg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220976066?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/dylan-hurd-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"97c82c0900d2f70036ab3ab047fc93ee69cd21a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/97c82c0900d2f70036ab3ab047fc93ee69cd21a3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/97c82c0900d2f70036ab3ab047fc93ee69cd21a3"}]},{"sha":"97c82c0900d2f70036ab3ab047fc93ee69cd21a3","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDk3YzgyYzA5MDBkMmY3MDAzNmFiM2FiMDQ3ZmM5M2VlNjljZDIxYTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"charlesgong-openai","email":"charlesgong@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T05:39:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T08:24:18Z"},"message":"Restrict plugin migration to home scope (#39663)\n\n## Why\n\nPlugin imports persist user-global enabled state. Repository-controlled settings\nmust not be allowed to select executable plugin content for installation.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Detect plugin migrations only from home-scoped external agent settings.\n- Reject plugin imports with a non-empty project `cwd` before loading Codex\n  configuration, while continuing to treat an empty `cwd` as home scope.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Cover repository-scoped detection with remote, installed, and project-relative\n  marketplaces.\n- Verify that forged project-scoped imports fail without writing `config.toml`.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 53cb46ae049cb49283187312d475d40cf42e35ab","tree":{"sha":"923dcb199949bcf89270c8df444969c726e4f25e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/923dcb199949bcf89270c8df444969c726e4f25e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/97c82c0900d2f70036ab3ab047fc93ee69cd21a3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/97c82c0900d2f70036ab3ab047fc93ee69cd21a3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/97c82c0900d2f70036ab3ab047fc93ee69cd21a3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/97c82c0900d2f70036ab3ab047fc93ee69cd21a3/comments","author":{"login":"charlesgong-openai","id":200841148,"node_id":"U_kgDOC_iXvA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200841148?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/charlesgong-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"240bbfc14ac46e30f56fa4e8c8f1ec34c4bc1cf7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/240bbfc14ac46e30f56fa4e8c8f1ec34c4bc1cf7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/240bbfc14ac46e30f56fa4e8c8f1ec34c4bc1cf7"}]},{"sha":"240bbfc14ac46e30f56fa4e8c8f1ec34c4bc1cf7","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDI0MGJiZmMxNGFjNDZlMzBmNTZmYTRlOGM4ZjFlYzM0YzRiYzFjZjc","commit":{"author":{"name":"ianw-oai","email":"ianw@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T04:59:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T08:20:08Z"},"message":"Add max and ultra reasoning efforts to the SDKs (#39662)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add `max` and `ultra` to the TypeScript `ModelReasoningEffort` type.\n- Add matching Python `ReasoningEffort` members and preserve them when SDK artifacts are regenerated.\n- Update the Python model-selection examples to rank the new effort levels.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Cover serialization of both new Python enum members while continuing to accept unknown future values.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 1412b77bdbb2530f5d38921cdea971dd34458353","tree":{"sha":"52697ffe6ca6e31e089afa129c79d45fd7086b02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/52697ffe6ca6e31e089afa129c79d45fd7086b02"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/240bbfc14ac46e30f56fa4e8c8f1ec34c4bc1cf7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/240bbfc14ac46e30f56fa4e8c8f1ec34c4bc1cf7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/240bbfc14ac46e30f56fa4e8c8f1ec34c4bc1cf7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/240bbfc14ac46e30f56fa4e8c8f1ec34c4bc1cf7/comments","author":{"login":"ianw-oai","id":269041055,"node_id":"U_kgDOEAk9nw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/269041055?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ianw-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/ianw-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ianw-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ianw-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ianw-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ianw-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ianw-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ianw-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ianw-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ianw-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ianw-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"631d5a8b02d417802b4674dbcd9f1a73dfec468c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/631d5a8b02d417802b4674dbcd9f1a73dfec468c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/631d5a8b02d417802b4674dbcd9f1a73dfec468c"}]},{"sha":"631d5a8b02d417802b4674dbcd9f1a73dfec468c","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDYzMWQ1YThiMDJkNDE3ODAyYjQ2NzRkYmNkOWYxYTczZGZlYzQ2OGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Benjamin Carlsson","email":"bc@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T04:58:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T08:13:56Z"},"message":"Expand Vim change commands and add character replacement (#39661)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add the configurable `vim_normal.replace_char` action, bound to `r` by default, to replace the grapheme under the cursor while remaining in normal mode.\n- Support change-operator motions such as `cw`, `c$`, `cj`, and `ck`, plus the repeated `cc` command for changing the current line.\n- Let `Esc` cancel a pending replacement before it reaches composer-level handling.\n- Preserve existing custom Vim bindings and chord prefixes when introducing the new default.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Cover replacement, grapheme boundaries, remapping and unbinding, change motions, cancellation, keymap conflicts, and keymap picker snapshots.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 98feb4eeb57142c37adb73abfe58d1f703b9270d","tree":{"sha":"a00ab822bdde812b4ac4b776393de53a482a9a25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a00ab822bdde812b4ac4b776393de53a482a9a25"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/631d5a8b02d417802b4674dbcd9f1a73dfec468c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/631d5a8b02d417802b4674dbcd9f1a73dfec468c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/631d5a8b02d417802b4674dbcd9f1a73dfec468c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/631d5a8b02d417802b4674dbcd9f1a73dfec468c/comments","author":{"login":"bc-openai","id":185964850,"node_id":"U_kgDOCxWZMg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/185964850?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/bc-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"e3e5ad28470f6a225301518c30a66e749a880164","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e3e5ad28470f6a225301518c30a66e749a880164","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e3e5ad28470f6a225301518c30a66e749a880164"}]},{"sha":"e3e5ad28470f6a225301518c30a66e749a880164","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGUzZTVhZDI4NDcwZjZhMjI1MzAxNTE4YzMwYTY2ZTc0OWE4ODAxNjQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T04:57:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T08:10:08Z"},"message":"Harden unsandboxed patch filesystem access (#39659)\n\n## Why\n\nAn `apply_patch` path can be replaced with a symlink after verification, allowing an unsandboxed patch operation to reach a different file than the one that was approved.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add `follow_symlinks` options to executor filesystem reads, writes, metadata lookups, directory creation, and removal, including the corresponding `followSymlinks` protocol fields.\n- Implement no-follow filesystem operations on Unix and Windows that reject links in any path component and restrict file access to regular files.\n- Run `apply_patch` with symlink traversal disabled when an otherwise-required sandbox is bypassed, while retaining the existing follow-symlink default for standalone callers.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Cover leaf and ancestor symlinks across patch add, update, delete, and move operations, including a path swap after verification.\n- Exercise local and remote no-follow filesystem behavior, concurrent directory creation, special-file rejection, and Windows reparse points.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 43fd479084891493ce13564fbd894b98f329c6dd","tree":{"sha":"f4b5646c59b84ac1ac47681ff59900e103731dba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f4b5646c59b84ac1ac47681ff59900e103731dba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e3e5ad28470f6a225301518c30a66e749a880164","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e3e5ad28470f6a225301518c30a66e749a880164","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e3e5ad28470f6a225301518c30a66e749a880164","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e3e5ad28470f6a225301518c30a66e749a880164/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"4e1a772a7dab609ca85ac9c6133a3e3f9fd30f48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4e1a772a7dab609ca85ac9c6133a3e3f9fd30f48","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4e1a772a7dab609ca85ac9c6133a3e3f9fd30f48"}]},{"sha":"4e1a772a7dab609ca85ac9c6133a3e3f9fd30f48","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDRlMWE3NzJhN2RhYjYwOWNhODVhYzljNjEzM2EzZTNmOWZkMzBmNDg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ankush Gupta","email":"amgupt01@gmail.com","date":"2026-08-20T04:50:06Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T08:07:06Z"},"message":"Let Guardian V2 satisfy required model reviews (#39658)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Allow the Guardian V2 approval monitor to handle reviews for models that require automatic review.\n- Preserve full Guardian review when Guardian V2 is disabled by configuration or managed requirements.\n- Cover required-model routing for low- and high-risk actions, plus both Guardian V2 disable paths.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: d1201cc3dbd7c4a07de633388b14f17ada9feb39","tree":{"sha":"26cc36900e00a42ed8fb5edb305133d271ada2e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/26cc36900e00a42ed8fb5edb305133d271ada2e3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/4e1a772a7dab609ca85ac9c6133a3e3f9fd30f48","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4e1a772a7dab609ca85ac9c6133a3e3f9fd30f48","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4e1a772a7dab609ca85ac9c6133a3e3f9fd30f48","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4e1a772a7dab609ca85ac9c6133a3e3f9fd30f48/comments","author":{"login":"ankushg","id":227041,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNzA0MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/227041?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankushg","html_url":"https://github.com/ankushg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankushg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankushg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankushg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankushg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankushg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankushg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankushg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankushg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankushg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"5e3a6fe4eee7bab705fed03b0dbed9bc110ef4cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5e3a6fe4eee7bab705fed03b0dbed9bc110ef4cd","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5e3a6fe4eee7bab705fed03b0dbed9bc110ef4cd"}]},{"sha":"5e3a6fe4eee7bab705fed03b0dbed9bc110ef4cd","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDVlM2E2ZmU0ZWVlN2JhYjcwNWZlZDAzYjBkYmVkOWJjMTEwZWY0Y2Q","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T04:45:12Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T08:02:39Z"},"message":"Warn when launching the deprecated MCP server (#39657)\n\n## What changed\n\nPrint a warning to standard error when `codex mcp-server` is invoked, noting\nthat the command is deprecated and will be removed in a future release. The\nserver continues to launch after the warning.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 0fefa2579a420a2fad85ef3afe373204f9836869","tree":{"sha":"d681cb6cce36e2b183ef619bd08db5dd2deeaa08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d681cb6cce36e2b183ef619bd08db5dd2deeaa08"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/5e3a6fe4eee7bab705fed03b0dbed9bc110ef4cd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5e3a6fe4eee7bab705fed03b0dbed9bc110ef4cd","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5e3a6fe4eee7bab705fed03b0dbed9bc110ef4cd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5e3a6fe4eee7bab705fed03b0dbed9bc110ef4cd/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"4a432d180dcd5db031a41ee8976a0a62735b1c77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4a432d180dcd5db031a41ee8976a0a62735b1c77","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4a432d180dcd5db031a41ee8976a0a62735b1c77"}]},{"sha":"4a432d180dcd5db031a41ee8976a0a62735b1c77","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDRhNDMyZDE4MGRjZDVkYjAzMWE0MWVlODk3NmEwYTYyNzM1YjFjNzc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T04:36:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T07:58:28Z"},"message":"Advertise the Desktop app in graphical Linux sessions (#39656)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add Linux-specific install and launch guidance to the generic and paid tooltip pools when `DISPLAY` or `WAYLAND_DISPLAY` is set.\n- Keep the Linux tooltip hidden in WSL and headless sessions, and preserve platform-specific macOS and Windows behavior.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Add coverage for native graphical Linux, WSL, headless Linux, macOS, and Windows tooltip selection.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: cbe9435db064d5718a591db363dcb7cc1429d5ee","tree":{"sha":"d4fd0e12b0c67c276db848c3311f128467563404","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d4fd0e12b0c67c276db848c3311f128467563404"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/4a432d180dcd5db031a41ee8976a0a62735b1c77","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4a432d180dcd5db031a41ee8976a0a62735b1c77","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4a432d180dcd5db031a41ee8976a0a62735b1c77","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4a432d180dcd5db031a41ee8976a0a62735b1c77/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"1802a65571e02e1d3e65afbbc6ec49abdc5c0495","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1802a65571e02e1d3e65afbbc6ec49abdc5c0495","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1802a65571e02e1d3e65afbbc6ec49abdc5c0495"}]},{"sha":"1802a65571e02e1d3e65afbbc6ec49abdc5c0495","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDE4MDJhNjU1NzFlMDJlMWQzZTY1YWZiYmM2ZWM0OWFiZGM1YzA0OTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T04:16:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T07:52:35Z"},"message":"Make core integration test permissions explicit (#39655)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Run local and remote compaction test turns with approvals disabled and an unrestricted permission profile.\n- Keep the full test harness available where compaction turns need the configured model and working directory.\n- Enable the Windows sandbox for managed-network unified exec process-event coverage.\n- Update request snapshots to reflect the resulting `danger-full-access` sandbox metadata.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 38eb46ca6ab28246d738e31eab900b2825072c7d","tree":{"sha":"c2eb59e5640239bcdfd97768142d05d863467cd9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c2eb59e5640239bcdfd97768142d05d863467cd9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/1802a65571e02e1d3e65afbbc6ec49abdc5c0495","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1802a65571e02e1d3e65afbbc6ec49abdc5c0495","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1802a65571e02e1d3e65afbbc6ec49abdc5c0495","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1802a65571e02e1d3e65afbbc6ec49abdc5c0495/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"7ece061767a8d0dea59757ca3285f7cb2ccfc4dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7ece061767a8d0dea59757ca3285f7cb2ccfc4dd","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7ece061767a8d0dea59757ca3285f7cb2ccfc4dd"}]},{"sha":"7ece061767a8d0dea59757ca3285f7cb2ccfc4dd","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDdlY2UwNjE3NjdhOGQwZGVhNTk3NTdjYTMyODVmN2NiMmNjZmM0ZGQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T03:49:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T07:48:46Z"},"message":"Enforce filesystem permissions when loading AGENTS.md (#39653)\n\n## Why\n\nProject instructions must respect the selected environment's filesystem read\npermissions. Tightening those permissions for a later turn must not allow\npreviously cached instructions to reach the model.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Apply each environment's filesystem sandbox while discovering and reading\n  `AGENTS.md` files.\n- Fail thread or turn setup when sandboxing blocks a discovered instruction\n  file, while allowing a restricted project with no instructions to start.\n- Clear cached instructions before refresh and include the Windows sandbox\n  level in the cache key.\n- Ignore inaccessible ancestor marker probes so readable instructions in the\n  selected working directory can still load.\n\n## Testing\n\nAdded coverage for restricted projects, denied instruction files, cache\ninvalidation after permissions tighten, and unreadable ancestor markers.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 6ea1a27b9c873a6260e4f87d42ae1317a6a4ae4b","tree":{"sha":"bc1f84c40c3cdca167da99eb71c3d1733cb75164","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/bc1f84c40c3cdca167da99eb71c3d1733cb75164"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/7ece061767a8d0dea59757ca3285f7cb2ccfc4dd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7ece061767a8d0dea59757ca3285f7cb2ccfc4dd","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7ece061767a8d0dea59757ca3285f7cb2ccfc4dd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7ece061767a8d0dea59757ca3285f7cb2ccfc4dd/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"ab82cddd049a4c72d3e23a1ebeb0c63c0d9c530b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ab82cddd049a4c72d3e23a1ebeb0c63c0d9c530b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ab82cddd049a4c72d3e23a1ebeb0c63c0d9c530b"}]},{"sha":"ab82cddd049a4c72d3e23a1ebeb0c63c0d9c530b","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGFiODJjZGRkMDQ5YTRjNzJkM2UyM2ExZWJlYjBjNjNjMGQ5YzUzMGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"zm-oai","email":"zm@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T01:37:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T07:42:18Z"},"message":"Resolve bundled Windows helpers through bin junctions (#39649)\n\n## Why\n\nInstaller `bin` directories can be junctions, so looking for bundled helpers\nrelative to the apparent executable path can miss the package's\n`codex-resources` directory.\n\n## What changed\n\nRetry bundled executable lookup from the canonical executable path when lookup\nfrom the original path fails.\n\n## Testing\n\nAdd a Windows regression test that creates a `bin` junction and verifies that\nthe sandbox setup helper is resolved from the package resources directory.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: f2f20ce1ccfa95ae65171a03a986d10e2560e696","tree":{"sha":"a8686640551986c99addd5ab23c9145527b1a2a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a8686640551986c99addd5ab23c9145527b1a2a5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/ab82cddd049a4c72d3e23a1ebeb0c63c0d9c530b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ab82cddd049a4c72d3e23a1ebeb0c63c0d9c530b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ab82cddd049a4c72d3e23a1ebeb0c63c0d9c530b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ab82cddd049a4c72d3e23a1ebeb0c63c0d9c530b/comments","author":{"login":"zm-oai","id":215741035,"node_id":"U_kgDODNvyaw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/215741035?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zm-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/zm-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zm-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zm-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zm-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zm-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zm-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zm-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zm-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zm-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zm-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"8aaf839774b90387b885f623efce95ec1bed8092","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8aaf839774b90387b885f623efce95ec1bed8092","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8aaf839774b90387b885f623efce95ec1bed8092"}]},{"sha":"8aaf839774b90387b885f623efce95ec1bed8092","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDhhYWY4Mzk3NzRiOTAzODdiODg1ZjYyM2VmY2U5NWVjMWJlZDgwOTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Dylan Hurd","email":"dylan.hurd@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T00:43:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T07:37:52Z"},"message":"Exercise restricted-token sandboxing in cyber policy tests (#39646)\n\n## What changed\n\nRun both branches of the heuristically safe command policy test with the\nWindows sandbox level set to `RestrictedToken`.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: ae5d754ec4a51d73a8e5f9d844f94a91f795fb72","tree":{"sha":"a974c62666dfc8f140750bc7e9f9f35489732d22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a974c62666dfc8f140750bc7e9f9f35489732d22"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8aaf839774b90387b885f623efce95ec1bed8092","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8aaf839774b90387b885f623efce95ec1bed8092","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8aaf839774b90387b885f623efce95ec1bed8092","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8aaf839774b90387b885f623efce95ec1bed8092/comments","author":{"login":"dylan-hurd-oai","id":220976066,"node_id":"U_kgDODSvTwg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220976066?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/dylan-hurd-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"af0e82c562a03aa748c3b56b2d772ad04a494bc7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/af0e82c562a03aa748c3b56b2d772ad04a494bc7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/af0e82c562a03aa748c3b56b2d772ad04a494bc7"}]},{"sha":"af0e82c562a03aa748c3b56b2d772ad04a494bc7","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGFmMGU4MmM1NjJhMDNhYTc0OGMzYjU2YjJkNzcyYWQwNGE0OTRiYzc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Anton Panasenko","email":"apanasenko@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T00:21:37Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T07:33:27Z"},"message":"Enforce managed residency for model providers (#39645)\n\n## Why\n\nModel provider configuration could override the residency header required by\n`enforce_residency`, so provider-backed requests did not reliably honor the\nmanaged setting.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Apply the managed residency header after building a provider, making it\n  authoritative for model requests and model discovery.\n- Warn when a provider configures the residency header through\n  `http_headers` or `env_http_headers`, while preserving the original provider\n  configuration and unrelated headers.\n- Cover HTTP and WebSocket requests, model discovery, and case-insensitive\n  header detection with targeted tests.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 461ef8989d5bd06ffdea694aee4265e392e07590","tree":{"sha":"eb3f553276e7bde59e7bb8ab72d7a06cb22dcb83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/eb3f553276e7bde59e7bb8ab72d7a06cb22dcb83"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/af0e82c562a03aa748c3b56b2d772ad04a494bc7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/af0e82c562a03aa748c3b56b2d772ad04a494bc7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/af0e82c562a03aa748c3b56b2d772ad04a494bc7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/af0e82c562a03aa748c3b56b2d772ad04a494bc7/comments","author":{"login":"apanasenko-oai","id":228802911,"node_id":"U_kgDODaNBXw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228802911?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/apanasenko-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"663da53823dfc923dc3b94233675b75feea98e59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/663da53823dfc923dc3b94233675b75feea98e59","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/663da53823dfc923dc3b94233675b75feea98e59"}]},{"sha":"663da53823dfc923dc3b94233675b75feea98e59","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDY2M2RhNTM4MjNkZmM5MjNkYzNiOTQyMzM2NzViNzVmZWVhOThlNTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"evanz-oai","email":"evanz@openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T00:12:06Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T07:29:43Z"},"message":"Sanitize developer context in full-history agent forks (#39641)\n\n## Why\n\nDeveloper messages can contain both inherited agent policy and unrelated context. Full-history forks need to replace the parent policy without dropping the unrelated content that shares its message.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Filter fork-specific developer instructions by content item instead of excluding an entire developer message.\n- Remove inherited multi-agent mode instructions before applying the child agent's current mode.\n- Preserve unrelated content items and discard developer messages only when filtering leaves them empty.\n\n## Testing\n\nExtend agent-control and subagent notification tests to cover compound compacted messages, multi-agent mode instructions, and proactive-to-explicit mode transitions.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 028834e237d8636c13b17a724574bc8eb09a55ba","tree":{"sha":"e9f1eb6064cff124211e6584768520c1952c05ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e9f1eb6064cff124211e6584768520c1952c05ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/663da53823dfc923dc3b94233675b75feea98e59","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/663da53823dfc923dc3b94233675b75feea98e59","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/663da53823dfc923dc3b94233675b75feea98e59","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/663da53823dfc923dc3b94233675b75feea98e59/comments","author":{"login":"evanz-oai","id":226170486,"node_id":"U_kgDODXsWdg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/226170486?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/evanz-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/evanz-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evanz-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evanz-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evanz-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evanz-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evanz-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evanz-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evanz-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evanz-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evanz-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"d944ce83a230eab293b2a7bd583466256227a74a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d944ce83a230eab293b2a7bd583466256227a74a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d944ce83a230eab293b2a7bd583466256227a74a"}]},{"sha":"d944ce83a230eab293b2a7bd583466256227a74a","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGQ5NDRjZTgzYTIzMGVhYjI5M2IyYTdiZDU4MzQ2NjI1NjIyN2E3NGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Jeremy Rose","email":"172423086+nornagon-openai@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-08-20T00:04:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T07:25:40Z"},"message":"Prompt to unarchive sessions before resuming or forking (#39640)\n\n## Why\n\nStarting an archived session with `codex resume` or `codex fork` stopped with\nguidance to run a separate `codex unarchive` command first.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Detect archived-session startup failures and offer to unarchive and retry the\n  requested operation.\n- Allow the user to cancel without modifying the archived session.\n- Render the confirmation in the alternate screen when available and preserve\n  inline terminal context when `--no-alt-screen` is set.\n- Preserve `--no-alt-screen` whether it appears before or after the `resume` or\n  `fork` subcommand.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Cover confirmation, cancellation, retry behavior, and unrelated startup\n  failures for both resume and fork.\n- Add prompt interaction and terminal rendering coverage, including narrow and\n  inline viewports.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 382cdbd15b5d12c091e554d6d3a2f9b3589654f4","tree":{"sha":"364bed859f572efca8432de942b4e6f2527d78cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/364bed859f572efca8432de942b4e6f2527d78cf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/d944ce83a230eab293b2a7bd583466256227a74a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d944ce83a230eab293b2a7bd583466256227a74a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d944ce83a230eab293b2a7bd583466256227a74a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d944ce83a230eab293b2a7bd583466256227a74a/comments","author":{"login":"nornagon-openai","id":172423086,"node_id":"U_kgDOCkb3rg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/172423086?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/nornagon-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"fdc23b93b895ecb8f0176c61822fc36e770c3b6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fdc23b93b895ecb8f0176c61822fc36e770c3b6b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/fdc23b93b895ecb8f0176c61822fc36e770c3b6b"}]},{"sha":"fdc23b93b895ecb8f0176c61822fc36e770c3b6b","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGZkYzIzYjkzYjg5NWVjYjhmMDE3NmM2MTgyMmZjMzZlNzcwYzNiNmI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Alvin","email":"alvinf@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T23:50:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T07:21:24Z"},"message":"Treat `invalid_grant` refresh failures as permanent (#39637)\n\n## Why\n\nOAuth token endpoints can report an unusable refresh token with the standard\n`invalid_grant` error instead of a legacy expired, reused, or revoked subtype.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Classify `400 Bad Request` responses with an `invalid_grant` error code as\n  permanent refresh failures, preserving the generic failure reason.\n- Cache that failure so subsequent refresh attempts do not repeat the request.\n- Keep other `400 Bad Request` errors transient and retryable.\n\n## Testing\n\nAdded refresh tests covering terminal `invalid_grant` responses and retryable\n`invalid_request` responses.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 513d34b514a7e4118a70c76e9d0fe779c006d5d8","tree":{"sha":"6df54f19626ff6c7061b15c49ce541a9ee25b89f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/6df54f19626ff6c7061b15c49ce541a9ee25b89f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/fdc23b93b895ecb8f0176c61822fc36e770c3b6b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fdc23b93b895ecb8f0176c61822fc36e770c3b6b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/fdc23b93b895ecb8f0176c61822fc36e770c3b6b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fdc23b93b895ecb8f0176c61822fc36e770c3b6b/comments","author":{"login":"ALVINF-OAI","id":301009192,"node_id":"U_kgDOEfEJKA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301009192?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ALVINF-OAI","html_url":"https://github.com/ALVINF-OAI","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ALVINF-OAI/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ALVINF-OAI/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ALVINF-OAI/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ALVINF-OAI/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ALVINF-OAI/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ALVINF-OAI/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ALVINF-OAI/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ALVINF-OAI/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ALVINF-OAI/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"7edd0a4c9dc69923e27a4948407971c8ca15db29","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7edd0a4c9dc69923e27a4948407971c8ca15db29","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7edd0a4c9dc69923e27a4948407971c8ca15db29"}]},{"sha":"7edd0a4c9dc69923e27a4948407971c8ca15db29","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDdlZGQwYTRjOWRjNjk5MjNlMjdhNDk0ODQwNzk3MWM4Y2ExNWRiMjk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Dylan Hurd","email":"dylan.hurd@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T23:45:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T07:17:31Z"},"message":"Show strict review warnings in the TUI (#39635)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Render `StrictReviewRequired` notifications as warning history cells that explain tool calls may take extra time.\n- Preserve the active command and task-running state when the notification arrives.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Add a TUI snapshot test covering the warning and continued command output.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: bf01b612a22b537b247b6df6818080fc73b5414d","tree":{"sha":"916884a37d69ba5ca1eb8ab915fbc1a9c9d6a141","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/916884a37d69ba5ca1eb8ab915fbc1a9c9d6a141"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/7edd0a4c9dc69923e27a4948407971c8ca15db29","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7edd0a4c9dc69923e27a4948407971c8ca15db29","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7edd0a4c9dc69923e27a4948407971c8ca15db29","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7edd0a4c9dc69923e27a4948407971c8ca15db29/comments","author":{"login":"dylan-hurd-oai","id":220976066,"node_id":"U_kgDODSvTwg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220976066?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/dylan-hurd-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"7ea7b293696473a12ea48701e8f638fa6bb2aed0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7ea7b293696473a12ea48701e8f638fa6bb2aed0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7ea7b293696473a12ea48701e8f638fa6bb2aed0"}]},{"sha":"7ea7b293696473a12ea48701e8f638fa6bb2aed0","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDdlYTdiMjkzNjk2NDczYTEyZWE0ODcwMWU4ZjYzOGZhNmJiMmFlZDA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Sean Huang","email":"seanh@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T23:38:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T07:11:46Z"},"message":"Expose permission profile resolution in the core API (#39632)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add `Config::resolve_permission_profile` to resolve named profiles from the\n  effective configuration and managed requirements.\n- Make active-profile network proxy lookup public and re-export\n  `CodexThreadSettingsOverrides` from `codex-core-api`.\n- Cover configured and managed profile inheritance, duplicate-name rejection,\n  and preservation of managed network settings.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: ffb5f54a932ef1a4b624677b5f051ecdcd1134b8","tree":{"sha":"5fab3232e08bf5d3e4b14ed77b7806f5b49ba8d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/5fab3232e08bf5d3e4b14ed77b7806f5b49ba8d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/7ea7b293696473a12ea48701e8f638fa6bb2aed0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7ea7b293696473a12ea48701e8f638fa6bb2aed0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7ea7b293696473a12ea48701e8f638fa6bb2aed0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7ea7b293696473a12ea48701e8f638fa6bb2aed0/comments","author":{"login":"seanh-oai","id":309889850,"node_id":"U_kgDOEniLOg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/309889850?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanh-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/seanh-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanh-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanh-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanh-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanh-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanh-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanh-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanh-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanh-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seanh-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"910ecccf30ba051efe5e5060dc8ccc644c554c7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/910ecccf30ba051efe5e5060dc8ccc644c554c7c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/910ecccf30ba051efe5e5060dc8ccc644c554c7c"}]},{"sha":"910ecccf30ba051efe5e5060dc8ccc644c554c7c","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDkxMGVjY2NmMzBiYTA1MWVmZTVlNTA2MGRjOGNjYzY0NGM1NTRjN2M","commit":{"author":{"name":"Dylan Hurd","email":"dylan.hurd@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T23:08:45Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T07:08:31Z"},"message":"Skip sandboxed shell commands in Guardian v2 by default (#39631)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Exclude sandboxed `exec_command` and `shell_command` calls from Guardian v2 classification by default while continuing to classify calls that request `require_escalated` permissions.\n- Add `guardianv2.review_scope.sandboxed_exec_commands` to opt sandboxed shell commands back into classification.\n- Keep other tools and namespaced shell tools in scope, and advance tool-call progress when a call is skipped.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Cover the default and configured review scopes, tool namespaces, permission modes, and skipped-call progress tracking.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 32fb540c69959b9a82569f0f2fc76b5517496e6b","tree":{"sha":"2404d52ac339e43817cb4cfbc5385bf65a0732ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2404d52ac339e43817cb4cfbc5385bf65a0732ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/910ecccf30ba051efe5e5060dc8ccc644c554c7c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/910ecccf30ba051efe5e5060dc8ccc644c554c7c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/910ecccf30ba051efe5e5060dc8ccc644c554c7c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/910ecccf30ba051efe5e5060dc8ccc644c554c7c/comments","author":{"login":"dylan-hurd-oai","id":220976066,"node_id":"U_kgDODSvTwg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220976066?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/dylan-hurd-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"942af8447b1d1addc81fb3c3135293497d479a06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/942af8447b1d1addc81fb3c3135293497d479a06","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/942af8447b1d1addc81fb3c3135293497d479a06"}]},{"sha":"942af8447b1d1addc81fb3c3135293497d479a06","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDk0MmFmODQ0N2IxZDFhZGRjODFmYjNjMzEzNTI5MzQ5N2Q0NzlhMDY","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T22:57:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T07:03:02Z"},"message":"Retire the untrusted approval policy (#39630)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Remove `untrusted` from the CLI, configuration schema, and MCP tool interface. Explicit `approval_policy = \"untrusted\"` settings now fail with an actionable error.\n- Remove the known-safe command allowlist. Projects marked untrusted now request approval for every command unless an explicit exec policy rule allows it.\n- Keep command parsing conservative by treating in-place `sed` forms as mutating and ignoring unrecognized commands when recording memory usage.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Cover rejection of the retired configuration value and approval requests for commands in untrusted projects.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: d6bf425edddfffbb325eee6acf383434af5fd33b","tree":{"sha":"f9d47db19312d1c3e52122a7a898b61f3a3589fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f9d47db19312d1c3e52122a7a898b61f3a3589fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/942af8447b1d1addc81fb3c3135293497d479a06","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/942af8447b1d1addc81fb3c3135293497d479a06","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/942af8447b1d1addc81fb3c3135293497d479a06","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/942af8447b1d1addc81fb3c3135293497d479a06/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"9ca99b51713066681cce211184c0ff9035496979","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9ca99b51713066681cce211184c0ff9035496979","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9ca99b51713066681cce211184c0ff9035496979"}]},{"sha":"9ca99b51713066681cce211184c0ff9035496979","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDljYTk5YjUxNzEzMDY2NjgxY2NlMjExMTg0YzBmZjkwMzU0OTY5Nzk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T22:26:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T06:57:00Z"},"message":"Preserve parent repository discovery through sandbox metadata mounts (#39629)\n\n## Why\n\nThe Linux sandbox represents missing protected metadata paths such as `.git`\nwith empty read-only directories. Repository and project discovery treated any\n`.git` directory as a checkout root, so this synthetic directory could hide a\nreal parent repository and its trust configuration.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Treat a `.git` directory as repository metadata only when it contains\n  `HEAD`, while continuing to recognize file-based `.git` entries.\n- Protect missing `.git` paths with the same read-only synthetic mounts as\n  other workspace metadata without disrupting parent-repository discovery.\n- Canonicalize and read-only bind the synthetic-mount registry into the\n  sandbox, and make protected-path cleanup handle read-only directory trees.\n\n## Testing\n\nAdded coverage for repository, project-root, trust, synthetic-mount, and\nLandlock behavior, including nested incomplete `.git` directories and a\nredirected `TMPDIR`.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 0724c54d56531143bb28011e4ca414cd3b0212be","tree":{"sha":"9cc995a17db6756a972a83cc84af3c7be8c9f77c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/9cc995a17db6756a972a83cc84af3c7be8c9f77c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/9ca99b51713066681cce211184c0ff9035496979","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9ca99b51713066681cce211184c0ff9035496979","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9ca99b51713066681cce211184c0ff9035496979","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9ca99b51713066681cce211184c0ff9035496979/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"e396ef3fc1bcb39fc857f255940623420ce2fc5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e396ef3fc1bcb39fc857f255940623420ce2fc5e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e396ef3fc1bcb39fc857f255940623420ce2fc5e"}]},{"sha":"e396ef3fc1bcb39fc857f255940623420ce2fc5e","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGUzOTZlZjNmYzFiY2IzOWZjODU3ZjI1NTk0MDYyMzQyMGNlMmZjNWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"philn-oai","email":"philn@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T22:24:33Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T06:52:01Z"},"message":"Add cwd-relative turn diff paths (#39625)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add the opt-in `cwd_relative_turn_diffs` feature.\n- When enabled, render turn diff paths relative to each selected environment's\n  working directory instead of the detected Git root.\n- Preserve repository-root-relative paths when the feature is disabled.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Cover enabled and disabled behavior for nested working directories across\n  supported originators.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 8b4908706a82b01f33ccd035b0945f9a29fce26f","tree":{"sha":"596b85f3ec37552836ffce540e0411e3cc65c159","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/596b85f3ec37552836ffce540e0411e3cc65c159"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e396ef3fc1bcb39fc857f255940623420ce2fc5e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e396ef3fc1bcb39fc857f255940623420ce2fc5e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e396ef3fc1bcb39fc857f255940623420ce2fc5e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e396ef3fc1bcb39fc857f255940623420ce2fc5e/comments","author":{"login":"philn-oai","id":295944085,"node_id":"U_kgDOEaO_lQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/295944085?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/philn-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/philn-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/philn-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/philn-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/philn-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/philn-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/philn-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/philn-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/philn-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/philn-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/philn-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"52e387dacaf5375d9fe5a77f7fc5f6fe31d2f610","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/52e387dacaf5375d9fe5a77f7fc5f6fe31d2f610","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/52e387dacaf5375d9fe5a77f7fc5f6fe31d2f610"}]},{"sha":"52e387dacaf5375d9fe5a77f7fc5f6fe31d2f610","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDUyZTM4N2RhY2FmNTM3NWQ5ZmU1YTc3ZjdmYzVmNmZlMzFkMmY2MTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Dylan Hurd","email":"dylan.hurd@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T22:04:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T06:47:30Z"},"message":"Prevent protected-path rename bypasses in macOS Seatbelt (#39623)\n\n## Why\n\nRenaming a writable directory could move protected descendants outside the\npaths covered by their read-only or unreadable policy entries.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Deny unlink-style writes to directory ancestors of protected paths, placing\n  these rules after broader write allowances in the generated Seatbelt policy.\n- Apply full write denies to unreadable glob matches and protect their directory\n  ancestors against renames.\n- Support brace alternation and backslash escapes when translating filesystem\n  globs into Seatbelt regular expressions.\n\n## Testing\n\nAdd coverage for ancestor rename attempts across explicit read-only and deny\nentries, multiple glob forms, canonicalized glob paths, and the new glob syntax.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: edfda9d4c2bc7ba2ecd6b67744446871e526084f","tree":{"sha":"00082ebce339dd935b64c683c8ef0851b4dcfa59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/00082ebce339dd935b64c683c8ef0851b4dcfa59"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/52e387dacaf5375d9fe5a77f7fc5f6fe31d2f610","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/52e387dacaf5375d9fe5a77f7fc5f6fe31d2f610","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/52e387dacaf5375d9fe5a77f7fc5f6fe31d2f610","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/52e387dacaf5375d9fe5a77f7fc5f6fe31d2f610/comments","author":{"login":"dylan-hurd-oai","id":220976066,"node_id":"U_kgDODSvTwg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220976066?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/dylan-hurd-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"f1e06b386510fbf5261cc3daebb164034918418f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f1e06b386510fbf5261cc3daebb164034918418f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f1e06b386510fbf5261cc3daebb164034918418f"}]},{"sha":"f1e06b386510fbf5261cc3daebb164034918418f","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGYxZTA2YjM4NjUxMGZiZjUyNjFjYzNkYWViYjE2NDAzNDkxODQxOGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T21:46:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T06:43:50Z"},"message":"Stream executor capability and skill file reads (#39620)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Use `ExecutorFileSystem::read_file_stream` for capability files and executor skill resources regardless of whether filesystem sandboxing is active.\n- Enforce per-file and bundle size limits incrementally as chunks arrive.\n- Preserve the existing error for Windows resources when the required filesystem sandbox is unavailable.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 1a40602a8f913588ec9a6ad7edd2d62eb82436e1","tree":{"sha":"ce407ad7ce16f693e9efe58f16c36a8277cb77d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/ce407ad7ce16f693e9efe58f16c36a8277cb77d7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f1e06b386510fbf5261cc3daebb164034918418f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f1e06b386510fbf5261cc3daebb164034918418f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f1e06b386510fbf5261cc3daebb164034918418f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f1e06b386510fbf5261cc3daebb164034918418f/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"da6e68951b985f9c45a472d8ced4b1d3935cc145","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/da6e68951b985f9c45a472d8ced4b1d3935cc145","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/da6e68951b985f9c45a472d8ced4b1d3935cc145"}]},{"sha":"da6e68951b985f9c45a472d8ced4b1d3935cc145","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGRhNmU2ODk1MWI5ODVmOWM0NWE0NzJkOGNlZDRiMWQzOTM1Y2MxNDU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Benjamin Carlsson","email":"bc@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T21:42:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T06:39:20Z"},"message":"Preserve inline TUI scrollback in Windows Terminal (#39619)\n\n## Why\n\nWindows Terminal can discard rows scrolled through a partial DEC scroll region instead of retaining them in terminal scrollback.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Detect Windows Terminal, including via `WT_SESSION`, and use full-screen scrolling for inline viewport growth and history insertion.\n- Keep the existing terminal-wrapped history behavior for Zellij while centralizing terminal-specific scrollback selection.\n\n## Testing\n\nAdd VT100-backed tests covering strategy selection and preservation of scrollback during history insertion and viewport growth.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 209a7a8053a1fcf911d6e0aee764e563b8725bd1","tree":{"sha":"095c8960d8d62d0a098b98316b04b5aaf2085f76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/095c8960d8d62d0a098b98316b04b5aaf2085f76"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/da6e68951b985f9c45a472d8ced4b1d3935cc145","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/da6e68951b985f9c45a472d8ced4b1d3935cc145","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/da6e68951b985f9c45a472d8ced4b1d3935cc145","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/da6e68951b985f9c45a472d8ced4b1d3935cc145/comments","author":{"login":"bc-openai","id":185964850,"node_id":"U_kgDOCxWZMg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/185964850?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/bc-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"4bb7804a23be9511e670e4622635c4717302abf9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4bb7804a23be9511e670e4622635c4717302abf9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4bb7804a23be9511e670e4622635c4717302abf9"}]},{"sha":"4bb7804a23be9511e670e4622635c4717302abf9","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDRiYjc4MDRhMjNiZTk1MTFlNjcwZTQ2MjI2MzVjNDcxNzMwMmFiZjk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Benjamin Carlsson","email":"bc@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T21:37:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T06:35:47Z"},"message":"Apply composer editing preferences to TUI text prompts (#39618)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Initialize custom text prompts with the main composer's editor keybindings and Vim setting.\n- Support Vim mode transitions, operator sequences, cursor styles, keymap contexts, and mode-aware footer hints in these prompts.\n- Start Vim prompts in insert mode, use the first `Esc` to enter normal mode, and preserve `Esc` cancellation outside Vim.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Cover remapped editor and Vim commands, mode and context transitions, paste handling, cancellation, and footer rendering at different widths.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 7a678310639dafb938084197df23d6d2a080a051","tree":{"sha":"3dd4611d08b8ffb22d6531d64f9b0e89e86f5fde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/3dd4611d08b8ffb22d6531d64f9b0e89e86f5fde"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/4bb7804a23be9511e670e4622635c4717302abf9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4bb7804a23be9511e670e4622635c4717302abf9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4bb7804a23be9511e670e4622635c4717302abf9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4bb7804a23be9511e670e4622635c4717302abf9/comments","author":{"login":"bc-openai","id":185964850,"node_id":"U_kgDOCxWZMg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/185964850?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/bc-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bc-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"bc3545b805de6e91a11b88114fe1673b678633ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bc3545b805de6e91a11b88114fe1673b678633ca","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bc3545b805de6e91a11b88114fe1673b678633ca"}]},{"sha":"bc3545b805de6e91a11b88114fe1673b678633ca","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGJjMzU0NWI4MDVkZTZlOTFhMTFiODgxMTRmZTE2NzNiNjc4NjMzY2E","commit":{"author":{"name":"Jeremy Rose","email":"172423086+nornagon-openai@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-08-19T21:15:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T06:29:32Z"},"message":"Validate linked worktrees before inheriting project trust (#39616)\n\n## Why\n\nA checkout could point its `.git` file at a trusted repository's worktree\ndirectory without proving that the repository had registered that checkout.\nThis could cause project configuration from an unrelated checkout to be treated\nas trusted.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Verify the linked worktree's `gitdir` backlink, `commondir`, registered\n  checkout, and main checkout ownership before resolving the main repository's\n  trust key.\n- Reject missing, oversized, symlinked, mismatched, or swapped Git metadata.\n- Preserve valid linked worktrees that use path aliases, separate Git\n  directories, or non-UTF-8 POSIX paths.\n\n## Testing\n\nAdd resolver and config-loading coverage for forged worktrees, metadata races,\ncase-sensitive paths, moved worktrees, and host MCP startup from project config.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 6052a7d10ad2d613436f20175c356abdef8c758e","tree":{"sha":"4cc1fe0d3418cf6c0f2b571992cc221bb58c901d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/4cc1fe0d3418cf6c0f2b571992cc221bb58c901d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/bc3545b805de6e91a11b88114fe1673b678633ca","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bc3545b805de6e91a11b88114fe1673b678633ca","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bc3545b805de6e91a11b88114fe1673b678633ca","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bc3545b805de6e91a11b88114fe1673b678633ca/comments","author":{"login":"nornagon-openai","id":172423086,"node_id":"U_kgDOCkb3rg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/172423086?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/nornagon-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"250b5ea2bff83edb151b29ca93248856c970126c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/250b5ea2bff83edb151b29ca93248856c970126c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/250b5ea2bff83edb151b29ca93248856c970126c"}]},{"sha":"250b5ea2bff83edb151b29ca93248856c970126c","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDI1MGI1ZWEyYmZmODNlZGIxNTFiMjljYTkzMjQ4ODU2Yzk3MDEyNmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Jeremy Rose","email":"172423086+nornagon-openai@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-08-19T20:48:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T06:25:17Z"},"message":"Bind MCP OAuth refresh tokens to their issuer (#39615)\n\n## Why\n\nAn authorization server discovered for an MCP server can change. A stored refresh token must not be sent to a different issuer than the one that originally granted it.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Persist the discovered authorization server issuer with new OAuth credentials and preserve it across refreshes.\n- Validate that issuer against a single pinned metadata snapshot before refreshing or adopting stored refresh credentials.\n- Require reauthentication when refresh credentials have no issuer or the issuer changed. An unexpired access token can still be used without exposing its refresh token.\n\n## Testing\n\nAdd coverage for issuer persistence, missing and changed issuers, metadata changes during startup, and refresh-token preservation.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 07e48ba892f627428a28bbed5cca4ad703e2a5fd","tree":{"sha":"24c75db037c169bad134dc61acfbd49edcb1a983","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/24c75db037c169bad134dc61acfbd49edcb1a983"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/250b5ea2bff83edb151b29ca93248856c970126c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/250b5ea2bff83edb151b29ca93248856c970126c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/250b5ea2bff83edb151b29ca93248856c970126c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/250b5ea2bff83edb151b29ca93248856c970126c/comments","author":{"login":"nornagon-openai","id":172423086,"node_id":"U_kgDOCkb3rg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/172423086?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/nornagon-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"530c1aed58b88060cfe851005c9dae3a89f44ad0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/530c1aed58b88060cfe851005c9dae3a89f44ad0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/530c1aed58b88060cfe851005c9dae3a89f44ad0"}]},{"sha":"530c1aed58b88060cfe851005c9dae3a89f44ad0","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDUzMGMxYWVkNThiODgwNjBjZmU4NTEwMDVjOWRhZTNhODlmNDRhZDA","commit":{"author":{"name":"sayan-oai","email":"sayan@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T20:47:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T06:21:54Z"},"message":"Prevent `apply_patch` from widening write permissions (#39614)\n\n## Why\n\nDeriving permissions from the parent of an already-writable patch target can\nunnecessarily grant write access outside the intended workspace.\n\n## What changed\n\nSkip targets already covered by the active filesystem sandbox policy before\nderiving additional parent-directory permissions. Targets outside the writable\narea continue to request the required parent access.\n\n## Testing\n\nAdded unit and CLI regression coverage for workspace-directory targets,\nalready-writable parents, and symlink escapes outside the workspace.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 187109ff0b56a1a399cb8a9981b7e822977025d5","tree":{"sha":"e90cd673c3d23e36fa3218abcc21aff3e242fad2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e90cd673c3d23e36fa3218abcc21aff3e242fad2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/530c1aed58b88060cfe851005c9dae3a89f44ad0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/530c1aed58b88060cfe851005c9dae3a89f44ad0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/530c1aed58b88060cfe851005c9dae3a89f44ad0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/530c1aed58b88060cfe851005c9dae3a89f44ad0/comments","author":{"login":"sayan-oai","id":244841968,"node_id":"U_kgDODpf98A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244841968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/sayan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"929e2b9c1d8a54c6409fada200440964e366ed39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/929e2b9c1d8a54c6409fada200440964e366ed39","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/929e2b9c1d8a54c6409fada200440964e366ed39"}]},{"sha":"929e2b9c1d8a54c6409fada200440964e366ed39","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDkyOWUyYjljMWQ4YTU0YzY0MDlmYWRhMjAwNDQwOTY0ZTM2NmVkMzk","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T20:45:32Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T06:17:48Z"},"message":"Harden MCP OAuth fallback credential writes (#39611)\n\n## Why\n\nThe fallback file contains OAuth credentials, so it must be private from the\nmoment it is created and writes must not follow links to another path.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Create the fallback file with mode `0600` on Unix before writing credentials.\n- Reject symlinks and other non-regular files on Unix and Windows, including\n  Windows reparse points.\n- Truncate and update an existing regular file through the validated file\n  handle, restoring private Unix permissions when needed.\n\n## Testing\n\nAdded coverage for creation under a permissive umask, updates through an\nexisting hard link, permission restoration, and symlink rejection.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: d3e4be52e8f4cebb66c59d496a7f77a952a2d0d9","tree":{"sha":"cb63f634f06cea676b8804483b2ca9202a16a7bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/cb63f634f06cea676b8804483b2ca9202a16a7bd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/929e2b9c1d8a54c6409fada200440964e366ed39","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/929e2b9c1d8a54c6409fada200440964e366ed39","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/929e2b9c1d8a54c6409fada200440964e366ed39","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/929e2b9c1d8a54c6409fada200440964e366ed39/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"c19482a7687ac0e53a113332e798a1b44f1dc773","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c19482a7687ac0e53a113332e798a1b44f1dc773","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c19482a7687ac0e53a113332e798a1b44f1dc773"}]},{"sha":"c19482a7687ac0e53a113332e798a1b44f1dc773","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGMxOTQ4MmE3Njg3YWMwZTUzYTExMzMzMmU3OThhMWI0NGYxZGM3NzM","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T20:25:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T06:13:28Z"},"message":"Limit Bazel integration test threads on macOS (#39609)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add a `test_threads` option to `codex_rust_crate` that sets\n  `RUST_TEST_THREADS` for sharded integration tests when configured.\n- Run the `core` and `app-server` Bazel integration tests with one Rust test\n  thread on macOS, leaving the thread count unchanged on other platforms.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 118147413eb141f557d9ee82858860617d61acce","tree":{"sha":"e8952a54e44a1d86ae057c9ce10758b02f261c41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e8952a54e44a1d86ae057c9ce10758b02f261c41"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c19482a7687ac0e53a113332e798a1b44f1dc773","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c19482a7687ac0e53a113332e798a1b44f1dc773","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c19482a7687ac0e53a113332e798a1b44f1dc773","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c19482a7687ac0e53a113332e798a1b44f1dc773/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"5c305eb50b3ebd12476c4bec6dc3de3c596b29a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5c305eb50b3ebd12476c4bec6dc3de3c596b29a2","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5c305eb50b3ebd12476c4bec6dc3de3c596b29a2"}]},{"sha":"5c305eb50b3ebd12476c4bec6dc3de3c596b29a2","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDVjMzA1ZWI1MGIzZWJkMTI0NzZjNGJlYzZkYzNkZTNjNTk2YjI5YTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"xl-openai","email":"xl@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T20:17:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T06:10:03Z"},"message":"Harden skill installation against unsafe symlinks (#39608)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Require selected skill paths to resolve within the cloned repository and reject\n  symlinked path components.\n- Reject special files and symlinks that escape the selected skill or resolve to\n  anything other than a regular file.\n- Add regression tests showing that escaping symlinks are rejected while links\n  to regular files within the skill are installed as file contents.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: d4c3f09fb630dea96b34ea5552de571b36f1ceca","tree":{"sha":"54a5f2f57023a1034970e133f3ad89790aee52df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/54a5f2f57023a1034970e133f3ad89790aee52df"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/5c305eb50b3ebd12476c4bec6dc3de3c596b29a2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5c305eb50b3ebd12476c4bec6dc3de3c596b29a2","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5c305eb50b3ebd12476c4bec6dc3de3c596b29a2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5c305eb50b3ebd12476c4bec6dc3de3c596b29a2/comments","author":{"login":"xl-openai","id":184293535,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvwYnw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184293535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/xl-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"186b449bc218ced20399bc950e23ca16cc3f9be3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/186b449bc218ced20399bc950e23ca16cc3f9be3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/186b449bc218ced20399bc950e23ca16cc3f9be3"}]},{"sha":"186b449bc218ced20399bc950e23ca16cc3f9be3","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDE4NmI0NDliYzIxOGNlZDIwMzk5YmM5NTBlMjNjYTE2Y2MzZjliZTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T20:14:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T06:03:25Z"},"message":"Resolve model-provided shells by type (#39607)\n\n## Why\n\nA model-provided shell path should select the requested shell type without\nallowing that path to determine which executable Codex runs.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Resolve model-provided shells through Codex's normal shell discovery and\n  fallback logic after detecting their type.\n- Keep the configured packaged zsh executable when the zsh-fork feature is\n  enabled and the file exists.\n- Update shell, unified exec, and network approval expectations to use the\n  resolved local executable and arguments.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: ebe6f7eec2cfd1c0548d5bf1a26b7a30dba02cc2","tree":{"sha":"e67c00df5258758d2e71b49a8216d3da36173d71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e67c00df5258758d2e71b49a8216d3da36173d71"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/186b449bc218ced20399bc950e23ca16cc3f9be3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/186b449bc218ced20399bc950e23ca16cc3f9be3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/186b449bc218ced20399bc950e23ca16cc3f9be3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/186b449bc218ced20399bc950e23ca16cc3f9be3/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"6869d17cc24fd30f7bedb4fa2969c31dbe81316a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6869d17cc24fd30f7bedb4fa2969c31dbe81316a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6869d17cc24fd30f7bedb4fa2969c31dbe81316a"}]},{"sha":"6869d17cc24fd30f7bedb4fa2969c31dbe81316a","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDY4NjlkMTdjYzI0ZmQzMGY3YmVkYjRmYTI5NjljMzFkYmU4MTMxNmE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T20:02:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T05:59:06Z"},"message":"Enable user namespaces in shared CI setup (#39606)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Enable unprivileged user namespaces for every Linux job that uses the shared\n  `setup-ci` action.\n- Disable AppArmor's unprivileged user namespace restriction when that sysctl is\n  available.\n- Remove the duplicate setup from the two nextest workflow jobs.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: a5aebe0795ada435e687826134411c8b1c28bd98","tree":{"sha":"2889c26cd897dd786c53a1f8eb31ddec734e7093","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2889c26cd897dd786c53a1f8eb31ddec734e7093"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/6869d17cc24fd30f7bedb4fa2969c31dbe81316a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6869d17cc24fd30f7bedb4fa2969c31dbe81316a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6869d17cc24fd30f7bedb4fa2969c31dbe81316a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6869d17cc24fd30f7bedb4fa2969c31dbe81316a/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"430bc36fb23575040ca22423f89ea8deac6bdf71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/430bc36fb23575040ca22423f89ea8deac6bdf71","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/430bc36fb23575040ca22423f89ea8deac6bdf71"}]},{"sha":"430bc36fb23575040ca22423f89ea8deac6bdf71","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDQzMGJjMzZmYjIzNTc1MDQwY2EyMjQyM2Y4OWVhOGRlYWM2YmRmNzE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T19:53:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T05:54:19Z"},"message":"Hide approved automatic review warnings in the TUI (#39605)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Ignore Guardian warning notifications that report a successful automatic approval review, keeping approved reviews out of TUI history.\n- Continue displaying all other Guardian warnings.\n- Extend the approved-review history test to cover the notification path.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 719e84bc5b20c0a5364d10f84be9c6ac96158719","tree":{"sha":"b1c153434081617cf9d8c03f079e92879ca22ec8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/b1c153434081617cf9d8c03f079e92879ca22ec8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/430bc36fb23575040ca22423f89ea8deac6bdf71","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/430bc36fb23575040ca22423f89ea8deac6bdf71","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/430bc36fb23575040ca22423f89ea8deac6bdf71","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/430bc36fb23575040ca22423f89ea8deac6bdf71/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"3434c2545b16487188effee3febf993c2d650b27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3434c2545b16487188effee3febf993c2d650b27","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3434c2545b16487188effee3febf993c2d650b27"}]},{"sha":"3434c2545b16487188effee3febf993c2d650b27","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDM0MzRjMjU0NWIxNjQ4NzE4OGVmZmVlM2ZlYmY5OTNjMmQ2NTBiMjc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T19:48:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T05:49:49Z"},"message":"Preserve queued TUI input semantics (#39604)\n\n## Why\n\nPaste placeholders and deferred slash-command parsing can hide the meaning of an input until it is expanded or a session is configured. Draining such input as an ordinary message can accidentally treat pasted text beginning with `!` as a shell command or lose `/plan` behavior.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Track paste-expanded inputs that begin with `!` as literal model input through history, queue editing, retries, and startup queues.\n- Defer `/plan` parsing when session or model state is unavailable, then submit it in plan mode with shell escapes disabled.\n- Drain queued input only after session configuration, and keep later queued prompts pending when an initial prompt cannot be submitted.\n- Suppress queue auto-send before applying a replayed thread session so input from the outgoing thread is not submitted during restoration.\n\n## Testing\n\nAdd coverage for direct, recalled, edited, interrupted, rejected, startup-queued, and plan-mode paste flows, including placeholder collisions and rejected initial images.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: d482220d8df21754f166fea5b54e9945f622a978","tree":{"sha":"8d880cffee197b103a03bc7e3f78693dbbd5d574","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/8d880cffee197b103a03bc7e3f78693dbbd5d574"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/3434c2545b16487188effee3febf993c2d650b27","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3434c2545b16487188effee3febf993c2d650b27","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3434c2545b16487188effee3febf993c2d650b27","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3434c2545b16487188effee3febf993c2d650b27/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"8e7f64697456d69809334652d86498c78d934dab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8e7f64697456d69809334652d86498c78d934dab","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8e7f64697456d69809334652d86498c78d934dab"}]},{"sha":"8e7f64697456d69809334652d86498c78d934dab","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDhlN2Y2NDY5NzQ1NmQ2OTgwOTMzNDY1MmQ4NjQ5OGM3OGQ5MzRkYWI","commit":{"author":{"name":"iceweasel-oai","email":"felixxia@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T19:36:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T05:45:13Z"},"message":"Use in-process parsing for PowerShell command classification (#39602)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Route PowerShell wrapper extraction and Windows safe-command classification through the tree-sitter lowerer.\n- Compile the PowerShell AST subprocess parser only in tests, where it remains available as an oracle.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 3690bc32e8987ac9de820ef39ff7401d98ea8d83","tree":{"sha":"b36f523bdd1cc41002502cdc91c4c5c815762dd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/b36f523bdd1cc41002502cdc91c4c5c815762dd1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8e7f64697456d69809334652d86498c78d934dab","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8e7f64697456d69809334652d86498c78d934dab","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8e7f64697456d69809334652d86498c78d934dab","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8e7f64697456d69809334652d86498c78d934dab/comments","author":{"login":"felixxia-oai","id":288149840,"node_id":"U_kgDOESzRUA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/288149840?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/felixxia-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixxia-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"198f42067aff70a55a0a42145aa5346c7597eac5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/198f42067aff70a55a0a42145aa5346c7597eac5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/198f42067aff70a55a0a42145aa5346c7597eac5"}]},{"sha":"198f42067aff70a55a0a42145aa5346c7597eac5","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDE5OGY0MjA2N2FmZjcwYTU1YTBhNDIxNDVhYTUzNDZjNzU5N2VhYzU","commit":{"author":{"name":"rka-oai","email":"rka@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T19:21:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T05:42:20Z"},"message":"Keep async user messages on the direct tool surface (#39601)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Register `send_user_message_async` as `DirectModelOnly` so supported models can call it directly without exposing it through code mode.\n- Exercise the async message flow with a code-mode-only model configuration and verify that the tool remains directly visible.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: ce22d5f63471ce90ac55ae2f3d0048f6cda57e01","tree":{"sha":"0ce0fc1a141da8b2d6db51438836f8df32fbd50f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/0ce0fc1a141da8b2d6db51438836f8df32fbd50f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/198f42067aff70a55a0a42145aa5346c7597eac5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/198f42067aff70a55a0a42145aa5346c7597eac5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/198f42067aff70a55a0a42145aa5346c7597eac5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/198f42067aff70a55a0a42145aa5346c7597eac5/comments","author":{"login":"rka-oai","id":240799229,"node_id":"U_kgDODlpN_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240799229?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rka-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"f6950546e5eaaf8c25031f1450920a6c0e43e103","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f6950546e5eaaf8c25031f1450920a6c0e43e103","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f6950546e5eaaf8c25031f1450920a6c0e43e103"}]},{"sha":"f6950546e5eaaf8c25031f1450920a6c0e43e103","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGY2OTUwNTQ2ZTVlYWFmOGMyNTAzMWYxNDUwOTIwYTZjMGU0M2UxMDM","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T19:13:21Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T05:36:23Z"},"message":"Protect macOS Seatbelt writable root anchors (#39599)\n\n## Why\n\nA sandboxed process could replace a writable directory root, changing the\nauthority boundary used to construct a later sandbox policy.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Deny unlinking or renaming directory roots granted write access by Seatbelt,\n  while preserving replacement and deletion behavior for writable files.\n- Reject writable roots with nested symlink components and report these as\n  Seatbelt preparation errors instead of network proxy failures.\n- Normalize writable roots before adding them to the generated Seatbelt policy.\n\n## Testing\n\nAdd coverage for symlink rejection, error classification, directory-root\nreplacement and rename protection, newly created roots, and writable file\nreplacement.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: ab1ed4e55f20034bc43e028e6529d3d1f0d8181c","tree":{"sha":"1d1dba7769b859f0e749d0d43386454b144ccdc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/1d1dba7769b859f0e749d0d43386454b144ccdc4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f6950546e5eaaf8c25031f1450920a6c0e43e103","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f6950546e5eaaf8c25031f1450920a6c0e43e103","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f6950546e5eaaf8c25031f1450920a6c0e43e103","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f6950546e5eaaf8c25031f1450920a6c0e43e103/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"d75c85f65139aa9245a96d05642a0a5d2bae436a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d75c85f65139aa9245a96d05642a0a5d2bae436a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d75c85f65139aa9245a96d05642a0a5d2bae436a"}]},{"sha":"d75c85f65139aa9245a96d05642a0a5d2bae436a","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGQ3NWM4NWY2NTEzOWFhOTI0NWE5NmQwNTY0MmEwYTVkMmJhZTQzNmE","commit":{"author":{"name":"sayan-oai","email":"sayan@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T19:11:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T05:29:12Z"},"message":"Separate thread settings from environment configuration (#39597)\n\n## Why\n\nEnvironment-owned permission profiles and workspace roots must remain effective\nwithout being persisted or restored as thread-owned settings.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Keep thread settings snapshots and restore data separate from the effective\n  configuration supplied by the primary environment.\n- Use resolved environment permissions, active profiles, workspace roots, and\n  network policy when building turn context and session events.\n- Preserve environment selections when agents are evicted, resumed, or spawned,\n  and validate owner configuration when it becomes ready.\n- Start memory initialization only after the primary environment is configured.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Extend remote-environment and multi-agent tests to cover settings persistence,\n  owner permission profiles, workspace roots, spawning, eviction, and resume.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: d82f126981cd0190233020bbdd61d96c70558868","tree":{"sha":"89fa79c0a17f4518a242eb6b5ab2d3a72a41d3bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/89fa79c0a17f4518a242eb6b5ab2d3a72a41d3bc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/d75c85f65139aa9245a96d05642a0a5d2bae436a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d75c85f65139aa9245a96d05642a0a5d2bae436a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d75c85f65139aa9245a96d05642a0a5d2bae436a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d75c85f65139aa9245a96d05642a0a5d2bae436a/comments","author":{"login":"sayan-oai","id":244841968,"node_id":"U_kgDODpf98A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244841968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/sayan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"8f4a48a6adc653359caaf02fd87a60b62fd7a702","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8f4a48a6adc653359caaf02fd87a60b62fd7a702","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8f4a48a6adc653359caaf02fd87a60b62fd7a702"}]},{"sha":"8f4a48a6adc653359caaf02fd87a60b62fd7a702","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDhmNGE0OGE2YWRjNjUzMzU5Y2FhZjAyZmQ4N2E2MGI2MmZkN2E3MDI","commit":{"author":{"name":"willwang-openai","email":"willwang@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T19:05:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T05:24:56Z"},"message":"Keep marketplace upgrade state out of config (#39595)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Stop writing `last_updated` and `last_revision` to marketplace entries in\n  `config.toml`; keep the activated revision in\n  `.codex-marketplace-install.json` instead.\n- Use installed marketplace metadata to detect up-to-date checkouts.\n- Snapshot the installed marketplace before activation and roll back a stale\n  upgrade if another installation changed the destination concurrently.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Verify marketplace add and upgrade operations leave `config.toml` unchanged.\n- Cover restoring a newer concurrently installed marketplace when a stale\n  activation is rejected.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 10942c3fc7c6c3f68b7d5953e8c1b5e86bf71866","tree":{"sha":"1677e5cdfea3667eedfef3e2631046c95207f4b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/1677e5cdfea3667eedfef3e2631046c95207f4b9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8f4a48a6adc653359caaf02fd87a60b62fd7a702","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8f4a48a6adc653359caaf02fd87a60b62fd7a702","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8f4a48a6adc653359caaf02fd87a60b62fd7a702","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8f4a48a6adc653359caaf02fd87a60b62fd7a702/comments","author":{"login":"willwang-openai","id":189043618,"node_id":"U_kgDOC0STog","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/189043618?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/willwang-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/willwang-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willwang-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willwang-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willwang-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willwang-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willwang-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willwang-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willwang-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willwang-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/willwang-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"1bfabb21fe56e21adce3aed945ab74aff27b67d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1bfabb21fe56e21adce3aed945ab74aff27b67d2","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1bfabb21fe56e21adce3aed945ab74aff27b67d2"}]},{"sha":"1bfabb21fe56e21adce3aed945ab74aff27b67d2","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDFiZmFiYjIxZmU1NmUyMWFkY2UzYWVkOTQ1YWI3NGFmZjI3YjY3ZDI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Angad Singh","email":"angad@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T18:29:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T05:21:09Z"},"message":"Raise the MCP tool name limit to 128 bytes (#39594)\n\n## Why\n\nThe Responses API accepts tool names up to 128 bytes, but MCP tool name\nnormalization limited model-visible names to 64 bytes.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Preserve MCP tool names up to the 128-byte Responses API limit.\n- Continue shortening and hashing names that exceed the limit so generated\n  names remain bounded and unique.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Cover names at the 128-byte boundary and immediately above it.\n- Verify distinct long names remain 128 bytes and code-mode compatible.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 75544d00e75dd0e9328b3e2ac763d26f9cc99a48","tree":{"sha":"2214ea28455681f8618af3d5afff4bb6e49ea882","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2214ea28455681f8618af3d5afff4bb6e49ea882"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/1bfabb21fe56e21adce3aed945ab74aff27b67d2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1bfabb21fe56e21adce3aed945ab74aff27b67d2","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1bfabb21fe56e21adce3aed945ab74aff27b67d2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1bfabb21fe56e21adce3aed945ab74aff27b67d2/comments","author":{"login":"angad-openai","id":175741063,"node_id":"U_kgDOCnmYhw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/175741063?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/angad-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/angad-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angad-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angad-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angad-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angad-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angad-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angad-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angad-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angad-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angad-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"493e0efb7b8867d668294418cd6cdddc01a740e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/493e0efb7b8867d668294418cd6cdddc01a740e0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/493e0efb7b8867d668294418cd6cdddc01a740e0"}]},{"sha":"493e0efb7b8867d668294418cd6cdddc01a740e0","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDQ5M2UwZWZiN2I4ODY3ZDY2ODI5NDQxOGNkNmNkZGRjMDFhNzQwZTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T18:19:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T05:16:59Z"},"message":"Prevent SQLx warnings from feeding back into SQLite logs (#39592)\n\n## Why\n\nWarnings emitted while querying SQLite or acquiring a connection must not be\nwritten back through the same SQLite log sink.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Disable the `sqlx::query` and `sqlx::pool::acquire` targets for the SQLite\n  log filter.\n- Keep warnings from other `sqlx` targets so useful diagnostics remain\n  available.\n\n## Testing\n\nExtend the log filter test to verify that query and pool-acquisition warnings\nare dropped while another `sqlx` warning is retained.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: cec9d4e07d113de8eccec7445ede0ae68e21886d","tree":{"sha":"27a437216e8c3c9ff299d5b30b3d4dcd4c652da0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/27a437216e8c3c9ff299d5b30b3d4dcd4c652da0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/493e0efb7b8867d668294418cd6cdddc01a740e0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/493e0efb7b8867d668294418cd6cdddc01a740e0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/493e0efb7b8867d668294418cd6cdddc01a740e0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/493e0efb7b8867d668294418cd6cdddc01a740e0/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"e7c0e8eb9f38db42e24b75cbfefcd53df88c82ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e7c0e8eb9f38db42e24b75cbfefcd53df88c82ce","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e7c0e8eb9f38db42e24b75cbfefcd53df88c82ce"}]},{"sha":"e7c0e8eb9f38db42e24b75cbfefcd53df88c82ce","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGU3YzBlOGViOWYzOGRiNDJlMjRiNzVjYmZlZmNkNTNkZjg4YzgyY2U","commit":{"author":{"name":"xli-oai","email":"xli@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T18:18:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T05:10:57Z"},"message":"Harden plugin manifest handling during installation (#39590)\n\n## Why\n\nPlugin installation skips symlinks while copying a plugin into the cache. A\nsymlinked manifest could therefore be used during source validation but omitted\nfrom the staged copy, allowing a lower-precedence manifest to take its place.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Require discoverable manifests and their parent directories to be regular\n  files and directories, rejecting symlinks and other non-regular entries at a\n  higher-precedence manifest path.\n- Verify that staging preserves the selected manifest path and contents before\n  activating the cached plugin.\n- Preserve generated fallback manifests by injecting and validating them in the\n  staged plugin.\n\n## Testing\n\nAdd coverage for symlinked manifest files and directories, precedence changes,\nand fallback-manifest staging.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 1b69c1e75cdfecb8cab4070a32aa9739833a70de","tree":{"sha":"b27db095ed860e33cccdfec6029a81b7e951d1fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/b27db095ed860e33cccdfec6029a81b7e951d1fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e7c0e8eb9f38db42e24b75cbfefcd53df88c82ce","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e7c0e8eb9f38db42e24b75cbfefcd53df88c82ce","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e7c0e8eb9f38db42e24b75cbfefcd53df88c82ce","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e7c0e8eb9f38db42e24b75cbfefcd53df88c82ce/comments","author":{"login":"xli-oai","id":270779301,"node_id":"U_kgDOECPDpQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270779301?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/xli-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"4b450d2f1b21e4e7d0baa0674f947b4ec6a02f14","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4b450d2f1b21e4e7d0baa0674f947b4ec6a02f14","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4b450d2f1b21e4e7d0baa0674f947b4ec6a02f14"}]},{"sha":"4b450d2f1b21e4e7d0baa0674f947b4ec6a02f14","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDRiNDUwZDJmMWIyMWU0ZTdkMGJhYTA2NzRmOTQ3YjRlYzZhMDJmMTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Dylan Hurd","email":"dylan.hurd@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T18:10:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T05:07:17Z"},"message":"Preserve unparsed shell wrappers in exec policy (#39588)\n\n## Why\n\nReducing a heredoc shell script to its inner executable lets a prefix rule for\nthat executable apply to the entire wrapper, even though the full script was\nnot parsed as a plain command.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Fall back to evaluating the complete shell wrapper when plain-command parsing\n  fails, including for heredoc scripts.\n- Keep these commands sandboxed when only the inner executable is allowed.\n- Propose the full wrapper as the exec policy amendment when approval is needed.\n\n## Testing\n\nAdded exec policy, Unix escalation, and approval scenario coverage for unparsed\nand heredoc shell wrappers.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 8f65133acb6b7c638263917e1d9137e45990772c","tree":{"sha":"81fbc08e3e3e88591a7a8f6d3595f91911ba5753","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/81fbc08e3e3e88591a7a8f6d3595f91911ba5753"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/4b450d2f1b21e4e7d0baa0674f947b4ec6a02f14","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4b450d2f1b21e4e7d0baa0674f947b4ec6a02f14","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4b450d2f1b21e4e7d0baa0674f947b4ec6a02f14","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4b450d2f1b21e4e7d0baa0674f947b4ec6a02f14/comments","author":{"login":"dylan-hurd-oai","id":220976066,"node_id":"U_kgDODSvTwg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220976066?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/dylan-hurd-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"3bebaea8f2091386b1e942a197adaf3c09b12c86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3bebaea8f2091386b1e942a197adaf3c09b12c86","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3bebaea8f2091386b1e942a197adaf3c09b12c86"}]},{"sha":"3bebaea8f2091386b1e942a197adaf3c09b12c86","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDNiZWJhZWE4ZjIwOTEzODZiMWU5NDJhMTk3YWRhZjNjMDliMTJjODY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Jeremy Rose","email":"172423086+nornagon-openai@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-08-19T18:06:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T05:03:49Z"},"message":"Isolate IPC in Bubblewrap sandboxes (#39586)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Pass `--unshare-ipc` when building Bubblewrap arguments for both restricted-filesystem and full-filesystem sandbox paths.\n- Update the Bubblewrap argument tests to cover the new namespace flag.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 61fb1d5150d09626a3b6ee7a9c6a508108c52e80","tree":{"sha":"8ee11f0ac85aba2e844585aed21315c907b6e801","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/8ee11f0ac85aba2e844585aed21315c907b6e801"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/3bebaea8f2091386b1e942a197adaf3c09b12c86","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3bebaea8f2091386b1e942a197adaf3c09b12c86","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3bebaea8f2091386b1e942a197adaf3c09b12c86","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3bebaea8f2091386b1e942a197adaf3c09b12c86/comments","author":{"login":"nornagon-openai","id":172423086,"node_id":"U_kgDOCkb3rg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/172423086?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/nornagon-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"6141747444deed4c42cd30f18dfa50a00268ca20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6141747444deed4c42cd30f18dfa50a00268ca20","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6141747444deed4c42cd30f18dfa50a00268ca20"}]},{"sha":"6141747444deed4c42cd30f18dfa50a00268ca20","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDYxNDE3NDc0NDRkZWVkNGM0MmNkMzBmMThkZmE1MGEwMDI2OGNhMjA","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T17:57:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T04:59:20Z"},"message":"Test plugin sync isolation from repository Git config (#39585)\n\n## Why\n\nThe pre-trust remote lookup must not inherit Git configuration from the\nrepository that launched Codex, where URL rewrites can invoke custom transport\nhelpers during an automatic plugin sync.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add a Unix regression test that runs the startup lookup from a repository\n  with a local `insteadOf` rewrite to an `ext` transport and verifies that the\n  helper is not executed.\n- Reuse `OPENAI_PLUGINS_GIT_URL` for the lookup so the production command and\n  regression fixture target the same remote.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: e53af4a82a4206c31bf0f4733f908dcc064a4795","tree":{"sha":"90da095e8ef0c1cbaa83473d2abbafef849ad6a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/90da095e8ef0c1cbaa83473d2abbafef849ad6a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/6141747444deed4c42cd30f18dfa50a00268ca20","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6141747444deed4c42cd30f18dfa50a00268ca20","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6141747444deed4c42cd30f18dfa50a00268ca20","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6141747444deed4c42cd30f18dfa50a00268ca20/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"8e2265196ecc03e08e816764fad7f1eaf49cbf4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8e2265196ecc03e08e816764fad7f1eaf49cbf4f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8e2265196ecc03e08e816764fad7f1eaf49cbf4f"}]},{"sha":"8e2265196ecc03e08e816764fad7f1eaf49cbf4f","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDhlMjI2NTE5NmVjYzAzZTA4ZTgxNjc2NGZhZDdmMWVhZjQ5Y2JmNGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T17:48:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-20T04:55:47Z"},"message":"Add a just recipe for assembling Codex packages (#39584)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add `just assemble-codex-package` as the documented entry point for the package builder.\n- Export `CODEX_REPO_ROOT` from `just` and release CI, and require the package builder to use it for repository-relative inputs.\n- Resolve the ripgrep and zsh manifests relative to their Python modules.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 039d12107a49171f064b0119adc6b99cf97c6c1e","tree":{"sha":"30f901e86fcb8649973b623c7ee8b39cbee97a3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/30f901e86fcb8649973b623c7ee8b39cbee97a3b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8e2265196ecc03e08e816764fad7f1eaf49cbf4f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8e2265196ecc03e08e816764fad7f1eaf49cbf4f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8e2265196ecc03e08e816764fad7f1eaf49cbf4f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8e2265196ecc03e08e816764fad7f1eaf49cbf4f/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"3b45c29062ff0e76e71c91b6753290400e7fa8da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3b45c29062ff0e76e71c91b6753290400e7fa8da","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3b45c29062ff0e76e71c91b6753290400e7fa8da"}]},{"sha":"3b45c29062ff0e76e71c91b6753290400e7fa8da","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDNiNDVjMjkwNjJmZjBlNzZlNzFjOTFiNjc1MzI5MDQwMGU3ZmE4ZGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"iceweasel-oai","email":"iceweasel@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T17:48:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T18:01:14Z"},"message":"Stop treating Git commands as inherently safe (#39524)\n\n## Why\n\nRepository configuration can cause even read-only Git commands to execute\nhelpers, so Git command arguments alone are not enough to establish trust.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Remove Git commands from the known-safe command classification on Unix and\n  Windows, including commands nested in supported shells.\n- Under the `unless-trusted` approval policy, require approval for commands such\n  as `git status` unless an explicit execution policy rule allows them.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Cover direct, shell-wrapped, absolute-path, and PowerShell Git commands.\n- Verify `git status` approval behavior with and without an explicit allow rule.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: dd04e0ddca0c56ba64ae64abe6e658bae7bf5a4d","tree":{"sha":"89ebe41835f85b9d75d5f36c16413ce2595e2b95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/89ebe41835f85b9d75d5f36c16413ce2595e2b95"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/3b45c29062ff0e76e71c91b6753290400e7fa8da","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3b45c29062ff0e76e71c91b6753290400e7fa8da","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3b45c29062ff0e76e71c91b6753290400e7fa8da","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3b45c29062ff0e76e71c91b6753290400e7fa8da/comments","author":{"login":"iceweasel-oai","id":234057055,"node_id":"U_kgDODfNtXw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234057055?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/iceweasel-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"1b450c79126cc56df29b833110a8c702f82de882","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1b450c79126cc56df29b833110a8c702f82de882","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1b450c79126cc56df29b833110a8c702f82de882"}]},{"sha":"1b450c79126cc56df29b833110a8c702f82de882","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDFiNDUwYzc5MTI2Y2M1NmRmMjliODMzMTEwYThjNzAyZjgyZGU4ODI","commit":{"author":{"name":"joeytrasatti-openai","email":"joey.trasatti@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T17:45:15Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T17:57:40Z"},"message":"Persist thread section moves before the first turn (#39523)\n\n## Why\n\nNew non-ephemeral threads have no persisted rollout or preview until their first\nturn, so moving them into a section could leave them absent from section-filtered\nthread lists.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Materialize and flush a non-ephemeral thread before applying an explicit\n  section move.\n- Include explicitly sectioned threads with empty previews in section-filtered\n  queries, and update the partial indexes to cover them.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Add an app-server test that moves a newly started thread into and out of the\n  pinned section before its first turn.\n- Cover empty-preview threads in recency and section-position query tests.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: aa3c4daf9890f06c08b93cd60f146099cbc6cfb2","tree":{"sha":"f56594d3ab00d16b5b6deabbeb66f8ec516c1b18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f56594d3ab00d16b5b6deabbeb66f8ec516c1b18"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/1b450c79126cc56df29b833110a8c702f82de882","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1b450c79126cc56df29b833110a8c702f82de882","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1b450c79126cc56df29b833110a8c702f82de882","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1b450c79126cc56df29b833110a8c702f82de882/comments","author":{"login":"joeytrasatti-openai","id":187452053,"node_id":"U_kgDOCyxKlQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/187452053?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeytrasatti-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/joeytrasatti-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeytrasatti-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeytrasatti-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeytrasatti-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeytrasatti-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeytrasatti-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeytrasatti-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeytrasatti-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeytrasatti-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeytrasatti-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"ffad92234000c3c0cf4b48cbf1e92c96b0ab5742","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ffad92234000c3c0cf4b48cbf1e92c96b0ab5742","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ffad92234000c3c0cf4b48cbf1e92c96b0ab5742"}]},{"sha":"ffad92234000c3c0cf4b48cbf1e92c96b0ab5742","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGZmYWQ5MjIzNDAwMGMzYzBjZjRiNDhjYmYxZTkyYzk2YjBhYjU3NDI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Charlie Marsh","email":"charliemarsh@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T17:23:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T17:34:00Z"},"message":"Isolate automatic plugin Git operations (#39520)\n\n## Why\n\nBackground marketplace and plugin refreshes can otherwise inherit repository-local or command-scoped Git configuration from the project that launched Codex. That configuration can redirect remotes or invoke Git helpers during an automatic operation.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Run automatic marketplace upgrades, plugin cache refreshes, and curated marketplace lookups with repository-scoped Git environment variables removed and a temporary trusted repository under the Codex home.\n- Carry the automatic/manual trust mode through marketplace upgrades and plugin materialization.\n- Preserve the caller's Git configuration for explicit marketplace upgrades, plugin installs, and refreshes.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Add regression coverage for repository URL rewrites, protocol helpers, command-scoped configuration, and manual Git filters.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 957f45fa3bd7ce7e1b83355f276cf65dc5e99c8e","tree":{"sha":"60703dc9583c25cf52aabd84cafa2b4e881584f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/60703dc9583c25cf52aabd84cafa2b4e881584f9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/ffad92234000c3c0cf4b48cbf1e92c96b0ab5742","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ffad92234000c3c0cf4b48cbf1e92c96b0ab5742","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ffad92234000c3c0cf4b48cbf1e92c96b0ab5742","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ffad92234000c3c0cf4b48cbf1e92c96b0ab5742/comments","author":{"login":"charliemarsh-oai","id":282065134,"node_id":"U_kgDOEM_47g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282065134?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/charliemarsh-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"18937b226524164546e7328a2ed47c0d52536e0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/18937b226524164546e7328a2ed47c0d52536e0a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/18937b226524164546e7328a2ed47c0d52536e0a"}]},{"sha":"18937b226524164546e7328a2ed47c0d52536e0a","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDE4OTM3YjIyNjUyNDE2NDU0NmU3MzI4YTJlZDQ3YzBkNTI1MzZlMGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Tamir Duberstein","email":"tamird@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T16:21:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T16:30:10Z"},"message":"Use `mem::take` to drain unified exec output buffers (#39515)\n\n## What changed\n\nReplace the custom `HeadTailBuffer::drain` helper with `std::mem::take` at\nthe output collection call site. This moves the buffered output out while\nresetting the shared buffer to its default empty state.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 7a93d1312f2cea0d7913a5264eeb01726b45e0ea","tree":{"sha":"ca370920a21c299d6ad667bc9f851a3872556593","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/ca370920a21c299d6ad667bc9f851a3872556593"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/18937b226524164546e7328a2ed47c0d52536e0a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/18937b226524164546e7328a2ed47c0d52536e0a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/18937b226524164546e7328a2ed47c0d52536e0a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/18937b226524164546e7328a2ed47c0d52536e0a/comments","author":{"login":"tamird","id":1535036,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MzUwMzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1535036?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird","html_url":"https://github.com/tamird","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"db675cc005db424855319cb1f86cc5c89700318d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/db675cc005db424855319cb1f86cc5c89700318d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/db675cc005db424855319cb1f86cc5c89700318d"}]},{"sha":"db675cc005db424855319cb1f86cc5c89700318d","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGRiNjc1Y2MwMDVkYjQyNDg1NTMxOWNiMWY4NmNjNWM4OTcwMDMxOGQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Tamir Duberstein","email":"tamird@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T16:10:25Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T16:20:21Z"},"message":"Use stored item types when materializing turn summaries (#39514)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Select user and agent summary items using the materialized `item_type` column.\n- Fall back to the type in `item_json` when `item_type` is empty so rows written by older clients still produce the correct summary.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Extend the summary materialization test to cover items inserted without a stored item type.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 45ca1107900e9b8d46561cea210a27ecd661cedc","tree":{"sha":"4cf5ab56e66f522d7a9f1198b4e1bdc732ffee47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/4cf5ab56e66f522d7a9f1198b4e1bdc732ffee47"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/db675cc005db424855319cb1f86cc5c89700318d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/db675cc005db424855319cb1f86cc5c89700318d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/db675cc005db424855319cb1f86cc5c89700318d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/db675cc005db424855319cb1f86cc5c89700318d/comments","author":{"login":"tamird","id":1535036,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MzUwMzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1535036?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird","html_url":"https://github.com/tamird","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"992f5c681f0d7aa25914686150f01e74820482d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/992f5c681f0d7aa25914686150f01e74820482d6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/992f5c681f0d7aa25914686150f01e74820482d6"}]},{"sha":"992f5c681f0d7aa25914686150f01e74820482d6","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDk5MmY1YzY4MWYwZDdhYTI1OTE0Njg2MTUwZjAxZTc0ODIwNDgyZDY","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T15:50:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T15:55:38Z"},"message":"Track built-in control tool calls in analytics (#39510)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Emit `codex_control_tool_call_event` for built-in control tools such as\n  `request_user_input`, `update_plan`, `view_image`, and goal tools.\n- Record correlation and timing metadata plus completed, failed, rejected, or\n  interrupted outcomes, and include these calls in turn-level tool counts.\n- Keep tool arguments out of control-tool analytics events.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Extend the app-server turn profile test to cover successful and failed\n  control tools, event correlation, turn counts, and argument exclusion.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: c20f73dfb79654e31b4b5040eddb0e0d91cae10d","tree":{"sha":"edba204aa2508de325c394da278ac63bb66d733f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/edba204aa2508de325c394da278ac63bb66d733f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/992f5c681f0d7aa25914686150f01e74820482d6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/992f5c681f0d7aa25914686150f01e74820482d6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/992f5c681f0d7aa25914686150f01e74820482d6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/992f5c681f0d7aa25914686150f01e74820482d6/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"6972c57c78aecedceff76413f866b333f0e63278","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6972c57c78aecedceff76413f866b333f0e63278","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6972c57c78aecedceff76413f866b333f0e63278"}]},{"sha":"6972c57c78aecedceff76413f866b333f0e63278","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDY5NzJjNTdjNzhhZWNlZGNlZmY3NjQxM2Y4NjZiMzMzZjBlNjMyNzg","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T15:09:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T15:47:56Z"},"message":"Test disabled enhanced Node REPL transcript images separately (#39509)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add a focused Code Mode integration test with Guardian transcript images enabled and enhanced Node REPL transcripts disabled.\n- Verify that the Guardian request and parent request omit both the screenshot and its surrounding transcript markers.\n- Remove this configuration from the broader parameterized transcript-evidence test.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 1309de12337a28a7e1d49eca509ba73207d4d9be","tree":{"sha":"d26bed9948065a839e0abfd55d95fad98efb5b4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d26bed9948065a839e0abfd55d95fad98efb5b4d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/6972c57c78aecedceff76413f866b333f0e63278","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6972c57c78aecedceff76413f866b333f0e63278","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6972c57c78aecedceff76413f866b333f0e63278","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6972c57c78aecedceff76413f866b333f0e63278/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"eb5a25aaa2288e7711b31087607aa5daf424e923","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/eb5a25aaa2288e7711b31087607aa5daf424e923","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/eb5a25aaa2288e7711b31087607aa5daf424e923"}]},{"sha":"eb5a25aaa2288e7711b31087607aa5daf424e923","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGViNWEyNWFhYTIyODhlNzcxMWIzMTA4NzYwN2FhNWRhZjQyNGU5MjM","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T15:09:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T15:42:22Z"},"message":"Test code mode notifications without a sync tool call (#39506)\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: 9ee4dfb93fee83737fa555bb6111101991417a4d","tree":{"sha":"bcfcba5221bc763939635d5c288c73863d235b48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/bcfcba5221bc763939635d5c288c73863d235b48"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/eb5a25aaa2288e7711b31087607aa5daf424e923","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/eb5a25aaa2288e7711b31087607aa5daf424e923","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/eb5a25aaa2288e7711b31087607aa5daf424e923","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/eb5a25aaa2288e7711b31087607aa5daf424e923/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"b0cdcce6169daf68cbd17f85f7688339eaf175ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b0cdcce6169daf68cbd17f85f7688339eaf175ef","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b0cdcce6169daf68cbd17f85f7688339eaf175ef"}]},{"sha":"b0cdcce6169daf68cbd17f85f7688339eaf175ef","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGIwY2RjY2U2MTY5ZGFmNjhjYmQxN2Y4NWY3Njg4MzM5ZWFmMTc1ZWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T15:09:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"copyberry","email":"copyberry@app.openai.com","date":"2026-08-19T15:37:26Z"},"message":"Test text stringify errors in the code mode runtime (#39505)\n\n## What changed\n\nMove circular-value coverage for the `text()` helper from the core integration\nsuite to the in-process code mode runtime tests. Verify that stringification\nreturns no content and surfaces the V8 circular-structure error without needing\na mock server or network access.\n\nGitOrigin-RevId: d506591af5ae8ce0a8c7305d633a7b0f2e458335","tree":{"sha":"c8a131f0556a692f5a612ac132dec8f009aea347","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c8a131f0556a692f5a612ac132dec8f009aea347"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/b0cdcce6169daf68cbd17f85f7688339eaf175ef","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b0cdcce6169daf68cbd17f85f7688339eaf175ef","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b0cdcce6169daf68cbd17f85f7688339eaf175ef","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b0cdcce6169daf68cbd17f85f7688339eaf175ef/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://